IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc1-common`
IMPORT `uc1-part1-introduction`
IMPORT `uc1-part2-age-and-place`
IMPORT `uc1-part2-education-and-commitment`
IMPORT `uc1-part2-finance-and-restrictions`
IMPORT `uc1-part3-awards`
IMPORT `uc1-part4-amounts`
IMPORT `uc1-part4-children-housing`
IMPORT `uc1-part4-needs`
IMPORT `uc1-part4-childcare`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), regulations 1 and 3 to 37 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions such a person asks: can I claim,
-- on what basis, how much will I get, and what must I do or tell the Secretary of State. Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from the core's lists), one for each
-- fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records the modules expect are built
-- inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here.
-- A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- REGULATION 2. For "terminally ill", "prisoner", "looked after by a local authority" and "foster parent" a question asks for the
-- facts the keel's record holds and calls the keel's rule (`reg 2 — terminally ill` and the others). Two places keep a plain yes or
-- no instead: regulation 8(4), whose Scottish limb asks its own fact about being looked after, and regulation 35, where the
-- foster parent is a childcare provider and not the person asking.
--
-- OFFICIALS. There is no seat for the Secretary of State. Where the regulations leave a judgment to the Secretary of State (that a
-- person lacks the capacity to accept a claimant commitment, that a request to extend the period for accepting one is reasonable,
-- that a charge is excessive, that a person has been referred to a scheme), the question asks the person whether the Secretary of
-- State has reached that view, as a fact the person can state.
--
-- FACTS OUTSIDE THIS TEXT. The Act, the Schedules (piece uc3), the rules on income and capital (piece uc2) and the capability for
-- work assessments (piece uc4) are not inputs of this layer. Where a question depends on them the person is asked for the result
-- ("Has the Secretary of State decided that you have limited capability for work?"), and NOTES.md lists them by the instrument they come from.
-- The figures the regulations themselves state (the amounts of regulation 36, the capital limit of regulation 18, the minimum amount
-- of regulation 17) are taken from the layer-1 modules and a later amendment would change these answers.

§ `Universal Credit Regulations 2013 -- the questions of a person who claims or receives Universal Credit`

§§ `The Regulations themselves (regulation 1)`

-- reg 1. The Regulations were made on 25 February 2013 and came into force on 29 April 2013.
@export Are the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 in force on a given day (reg 1)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 in force on a given day` IF
    `reg 1 — these Regulations are in force on a day` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Couples and the people I am responsible for (regulations 3 to 5)`

-- reg 3(2). A couple may be entitled as joint claimants although one of them fails the basic condition on age (4(1)(b)) or on
-- education (4(1)(d)), where the other meets the conditions that the paragraph names.
@export May my partner and I claim jointly although one of us is over the qualifying age or in education (reg 3(2))?
GIVEN `I am under the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under the qualifying age for state pension credit?
      `I am not receiving education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not receiving education (as the regulations define it)?
      `I am excepted from the education condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you excepted from the education condition by regulation 14 (see the question on that regulation)?
      `my partner is under the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner under the qualifying age for state pension credit?
      `my partner is not receiving education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner not receiving education (as the regulations define it)?
      `my partner is excepted from the education condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner excepted from the education condition by regulation 14?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my partner and I claim jointly although one of us is over the qualifying age or in education` IF
    `reg 3(2) — a couple may be entitled as joint claimants despite a basic condition` `me` `my partner`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `Member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(b) and (d)` WITH
            `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(b), under the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS `I am under the qualifying age for state pension credit`
            `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(d), not receiving education` IS `I am not receiving education`
            `is excepted from the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) by regulation 14` IS `I am excepted from the education condition`
        `my partner` MEANS `Member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(b) and (d)` WITH
            `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(b), under the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS `my partner is under the qualifying age for state pension credit`
            `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(d), not receiving education` IS `my partner is not receiving education`
            `is excepted from the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) by regulation 14` IS `my partner is excepted from the education condition`

-- reg 3(3). A member of a couple may make a claim as a single person where the other member is under 18 (and not within the age
-- 16 exception), is not in Great Britain, is a prisoner, is a person (other than a prisoner) to whom regulation 19 applies, or is a person to whom section
-- 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 applies.
@export May I claim as a single person although I have a partner (reg 3(3))?
GIVEN `my partner is at least 18 years old` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner at least 18 years old?
      `my partner is a person in respect of whom the minimum age in regulation 8 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner someone for whom the minimum age of 16 in regulation 8 applies?
      `my partner is in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner in Great Britain (as the regulations treat it)?
      `my partner is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction?
      `my partner is detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court?
      `my partner is on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner on temporary release in accordance with the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989?
      `my partner is detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner detained in hospital under the Mental Health Act 1983 or, in Scotland, under the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 or the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995?
      `my partner cannot be entitled because of regulation 19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner someone who cannot be entitled because of regulation 19 (for example a member of a religious order fully maintained by it)?
      `section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 applies to my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 apply to your partner (a person subject to immigration control who cannot claim public funds)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I claim as a single person although I have a partner` IF
    `reg 3(3) — a member of a couple may make a claim as a single person` `my partner`
    WHERE
        `my partner's detention` MEANS Detention WITH
            `detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction` IS `my partner is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction`
            `detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court` IS `my partner is detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court`
            `on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989` IS `my partner is on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989`
            `detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS `my partner is detained in hospital under the mental health Acts`
        `my partner is a prisoner` MEANS
            `reg 2 — prisoner` `my partner's detention`
        `my partner` MEANS `Other member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(a) and (c)` WITH
            `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(a), at least 18 years old` IS `my partner is at least 18 years old`
            `is a person in respect of whom the minimum age specified in regulation 8 applies` IS `my partner is a person in respect of whom the minimum age in regulation 8 applies`
            `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(c), in Great Britain` IS `my partner is in Great Britain`
            `is a prisoner` IS `my partner is a prisoner`
            `is a person in respect of whom entitlement does not arise by virtue of regulation 19` IS `my partner cannot be entitled because of regulation 19`
            `is a person to whom section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 applies` IS `section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 applies to my partner`

-- reg 3(1) to (3). The basis of the claim. This question takes, as plain yes-or-no answers, the results of the two questions above.
@export Do I claim as a single person or jointly with my partner (reg 3)?
GIVEN `I am a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple (married, in a civil partnership, or living together as if you were)?
      `the answer to the single-claim question is yes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "May I claim as a single person although I have a partner" give the answer yes?
      `my partner and I each meet all the basic conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you and your partner each meet all the basic conditions of entitlement?
      `the answer to the joint-claim question is yes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "May my partner and I claim jointly although one of us is over the qualifying age or in education" give the answer yes?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Claim basis`
DECIDE `Do I claim as a single person or jointly with my partner` IS
    `reg 3 — the basis on which the person claims` `I am a member of a couple` `the answer to the single-claim question is yes` `my partner and I each meet all the basic conditions` `the answer to the joint-claim question is yes`

@export Is our marriage a polygamous marriage (reg 3(5))?
GIVEN `a party to the marriage is married to more than one person during it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a party to the marriage married to more than one person during it?
      `the marriage took place under the laws of a country which permits polygamy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the marriage take place under the laws of a country which permits polygamy?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our marriage a polygamous marriage` IF
    `reg 3(5) — a polygamous marriage` `a party to the marriage is married to more than one person during it` `the marriage took place under the laws of a country which permits polygamy`

-- reg 3(4). In a polygamous marriage, the marriage is disregarded between two people if one of them has an earlier marriage that still subsists and the other party to that earlier marriage lives in the same household.
@export Is the fact that my spouse and I are husband and wife disregarded, so that I may claim as a single person (reg 3(4))?
GIVEN `we are parties to a polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and your spouse parties to a polygamous marriage (see the previous question)?
      `one of us is a party to an earlier marriage that still subsists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of you a party to an earlier marriage that still subsists?
      `the other party to that earlier marriage lives in the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other party to that earlier marriage live in the same household?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the fact that my spouse and I are husband and wife disregarded` IF
    `reg 3(4) — the fact that they are husband and wife is disregarded` `we are parties to a polygamous marriage` `one of us is a party to an earlier marriage that still subsists` `the other party to that earlier marriage lives in the same household`

-- reg 3(6). Members of a couple cease to be treated as a couple when one has been absent from the other for more than 6 months
-- (or is expected to be).
@export Do my partner and I stop being treated as a couple because one of us has been away (reg 3(6))?
GIVEN `the day the absence began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the absence begin?
      `the day to which the absence has lasted` IS A DATE @desc Up to what day has the absence lasted so far (today, if it is still going on)?
      `the day the absence is expected to end` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the absence expected to end?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my partner and I stop being treated as a couple because one of us has been away` IF
    `reg 3(6) — the members of a couple cease to be treated as a couple` `the absence`
    WHERE
        `the absence` MEANS `Absence that is measured against a limit` WITH
            `first day of the absence` IS `the day the absence began`
            `day to which the absence has lasted` IS `the day to which the absence has lasted`
            `expected last day of the absence` IS `the day the absence is expected to end`

-- reg 4(2) to (5). Whether a child or young person is my responsibility, before the exceptions of paragraphs (6) and (7).
@export Am I responsible for a child or young person who lives with me, apart from the exceptions (reg 4(2) to (5))?
GIVEN `the child or young person normally lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the child or young person normally live with you?
      `the young person is a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the young person a qualifying young person (see the question on regulation 5)? Answer no if it is a child.
      `the young person and I live as a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the young person living together as a couple?
      `the child or young person normally lives with two or more people who are not a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the child or young person normally live with two or more people who are not a couple?
      `I have the main responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, do you have the main responsibility, because you were nominated jointly or the Secretary of State decided it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I responsible for a child or young person who lives with me, apart from the exceptions` IF
    `reg 4(2) to (5) — the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person apart from paragraphs (6) and (7)` `the household`
    WHERE
        `the household` MEANS `Child or qualifying young person and the person who may be responsible` WITH
            `the child or qualifying young person normally lives with the person` IS `the child or young person normally lives with me`
            `the child or qualifying young person is a qualifying young person` IS `the young person is a qualifying young person`
            `the person and the qualifying young person are living as a couple` IS `the young person and I live as a couple`
            `the child or qualifying young person normally lives with two or more persons who are not a couple` IS `the child or young person normally lives with two or more people who are not a couple`
            `the person has the main responsibility, by nomination under paragraph (5) or by the Secretary of State's determination` IS `I have the main responsibility`

-- reg 4(6) and 4A(1). A child or young person is treated as nobody's responsibility while looked after by a local authority (except in the
-- periods regulation 4A(1) excludes) or while a prisoner.
@export Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner (reg 4(6), 4A(1))?
GIVEN `the child or young person is looked after within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person looked after by a local authority within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989 (England)?
      `the child or young person is looked after within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person looked after by a local authority within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 (Scotland)?
      `the child or young person is looked after within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person looked after by a local authority within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 (Wales)?
      `the period is a planned short break for respite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the period a planned short break (or one of a series) to give the person who normally cares for them a rest?
      `the child or young person is placed with or lives with their parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person placed with, or still living with, their parent?
      `the child or young person is placed with or lives with someone with parental responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person placed with, or still living with, someone who has parental responsibility for them?
      `the child or young person is placed for adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person placed for adoption?
      `the child or young person is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction?
      `the child or young person is detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court?
      `the child or young person is on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person on temporary release in accordance with the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989?
      `the child or young person is detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person detained in hospital under the Mental Health Act 1983 or, in Scotland, under the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 or the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner` IF
    `reg 4(6) — the child or qualifying young person is treated as not being the responsibility of any person` `a local authority looks after the child or young person` `the period is excluded` `the child or young person is a prisoner`
    WHERE
        `the care of the child or young person` MEANS `Care of a child` WITH
            `looked after within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989` IS `the child or young person is looked after within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989`
            `looked after within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995` IS `the child or young person is looked after within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995`
            `looked after within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` IS `the child or young person is looked after within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`
        `a local authority looks after the child or young person` MEANS
            `reg 2 — looked after by a local authority` `the care of the child or young person`
        `the child or young person's detention` MEANS Detention WITH
            `detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction` IS `the child or young person is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction`
            `detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court` IS `the child or young person is detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court`
            `on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989` IS `the child or young person is on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989`
            `detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS `the child or young person is detained in hospital under the mental health Acts`
        `the child or young person is a prisoner` MEANS
            `reg 2 — prisoner` `the child or young person's detention`
        `the period is excluded` MEANS
            `reg 4A(1) — the period is excluded from regulation 4(6)(a)` `the period is a planned short break for respite` `the child or young person is placed with or lives with their parent` `the child or young person is placed with or lives with someone with parental responsibility` `the child or young person is placed for adoption`

-- reg 4A(2). Parental responsibility, for the purposes of regulation 4A(1).
@export Do I have parental responsibility for the child (reg 4A(2))?
GIVEN `the nation of Great Britain where I live` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain do you live (England, Wales or Scotland)?
      `the nation of Great Britain where the child is placed with me` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the child placed with me (England, Wales or Scotland)?
      `the child is placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child placed with me under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (England) Regulations 2010, the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (Wales) Regulations 2015, or the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009 (whichever applies in that nation)?
      `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland: are you a foster carer or a kinship carer with whom the child is placed? (Any answer elsewhere.)
      `I have parental responsibility under section 3 of the Children Act 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In England or Wales: do you have parental responsibility for the child under section 3 of the Children Act 1989?
      `I have responsibilities or rights under sections 1 or 2 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland: do you have any or all of the responsibilities or rights described in sections 1 or 2 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have parental responsibility for the child` IF
    `reg 4A(2) — the person has parental responsibility` `the nation of Great Britain where I live` `I am a foster parent` `I have parental responsibility under section 3 of the Children Act 1989` `I have responsibilities or rights under sections 1 or 2 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995`
    WHERE
        `my placement` MEANS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
            `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation of Great Britain where the child is placed with me`
            `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `the child is placed with me under the placement regulations`
            `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer`
        `I am a foster parent` MEANS
            `reg 2 — foster parent` `my placement`

-- reg 4(7). A child or young person who is away from home for a time: when I stop being responsible for them.
@export Do I stop being responsible for a child or young person who is away from home for a time (reg 4(7))?
GIVEN `the day the absence began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the child or young person's absence from your household begin?
      `the day to which the absence has lasted` IS A DATE @desc Up to what day has the absence lasted so far (today, if it is still going on)?
      `the day the absence is expected to end` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the absence expected to end?
      `the absence is from Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person away from Great Britain?
      `a one month absence would be disregarded for regulation 11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence one of the kinds for which regulation 11(2) or (3) would disregard an absence of more than a month (for example, medical treatment)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I stop being responsible for a child or young person who is away from home for a time` IF
    `reg 4(7) — the person ceases to be responsible because of a temporary absence` `the absence` `the absence is from Great Britain` `a one month absence would be disregarded for regulation 11`
    WHERE
        `the absence` MEANS `Absence that is measured against a limit` WITH
            `first day of the absence` IS `the day the absence began`
            `day to which the absence has lasted` IS `the day to which the absence has lasted`
            `expected last day of the absence` IS `the day the absence is expected to end`

-- reg 4. Whether I am responsible for the child or young person. The three answers are those of the three questions above.
@export Am I responsible for the child or young person (reg 4)?
GIVEN `the answer to the household question is yes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Am I responsible for a child or young person who lives with me, apart from the exceptions" give the answer yes?
      `the answer to the local authority question is yes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Is the child or young person treated as nobody's responsibility because a local authority looks after them or they are a prisoner" give the answer yes?
      `the answer to the absence question is yes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Do I stop being responsible for a child or young person who is away from home for a time" give the answer yes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I responsible for the child or young person` IF
    `reg 4 — the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person` `the answer to the household question is yes` `the answer to the local authority question is yes` `the answer to the absence question is yes`

-- reg 5. A person who has reached 16 but not 20 is a qualifying young person up to, but not including, the 1st September following their 16th
-- birthday; and up to, but not including, the 1st September following their 19th birthday if enrolled on approved training or a non-advanced
-- course at a school or college (or provided elsewhere and approved by the Secretary of State) with more than 12 hours a week of tuition,
-- practical work, supervised study or examinations. At 19 the course must have started before that age. Education by a contract of
-- employment does not count, and a person receiving UC, ESA or JSA is not a qualifying young person.
@export Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day (reg 5)?
GIVEN `the young person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the young person's date of birth?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
      `the young person is enrolled on approved training or a course of education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the young person enrolled on, or accepted for, approved training or a course of education?
      `the course is a course of advanced education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a course of advanced education (a degree, a diploma of higher education, a higher national diploma, or above A level standard)?
      `the course is at a school or college or approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it provided at a school or college, or elsewhere but approved by the Secretary of State?
      `hours a week in term time` IS A NUMBER @desc On average, how many hours a week in term time does the young person spend in tuition, practical work, supervised study or examinations?
      `the young person started it before 19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the young person start the education or training (or enrol or get accepted for it) before reaching 19?
      `it is provided by means of a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the education or training provided by means of a contract of employment?
      `the young person receives universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the young person receiving Universal Credit?
      `the young person receives employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the young person receiving employment and support allowance?
      `the young person receives jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the young person receiving jobseeker's allowance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the young person a qualifying young person on a given day` IF
    `reg 5 — the person is a qualifying young person on a day` `the young person` `the day I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `the young person` MEANS `Young person and the education or training` WITH
            `date of birth` IS `the young person's date of birth`
            `the person is enrolled on, or accepted for, approved training or a course of education` IS `the young person is enrolled on approved training or a course of education`
            `the course is a course of advanced education` IS `the course is a course of advanced education`
            `the course is provided at a school or college, or elsewhere but approved by the Secretary of State` IS `the course is at a school or college or approved by the Secretary of State`
            `the average time spent during term time in tuition, practical work, supervised study or examinations` IS `hours a week in term time`
            `the person started the education or training, or was enrolled on or accepted for it, before reaching the age of 19` IS `the young person started it before 19`
            `the education or training is provided by means of a contract of employment` IS `it is provided by means of a contract of employment`
            `the person is receiving universal credit` IS `the young person receives universal credit`
            `the person is receiving` IS `the benefits the young person receives`
        `the benefits the young person receives` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the young person receives employment and support allowance` AND `the young person receives jobseeker's allowance` THEN LIST `employment and support allowance`, `jobseeker's allowance`
                IF `the young person receives employment and support allowance` THEN LIST `employment and support allowance`
                IF `the young person receives jobseeker's allowance` THEN LIST `jobseeker's allowance`
                OTHERWISE EMPTY

§§ `Rounding (regulation 6)`

-- reg 6(2). Rounding does not apply to the daily rate of a reduction under section 26 or 27 of the Act in regulation 111.
@export Does the rounding rule apply to my calculation (reg 6(2))?
GIVEN `the calculation is the daily rate for a reduction under section 26 or 27 of the Act in regulation 111` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the calculation the daily rate for a reduction under section 26 or 27 of the Act, in regulation 111?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the rounding rule apply to my calculation` IF
    `reg 6(2) — regulation 6 applies to the calculation` `the calculation is the daily rate for a reduction under section 26 or 27 of the Act in regulation 111`

§§ `Whether I can be entitled (regulation 7)`

-- reg 7. This regulation only introduces the Part: the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act (regulations 8 to 16), the financial conditions in section 5 (regulations 17 and 18), and cases where no entitlement arises even if both are met (regulation 19). The question joins the three: entitlement can arise where the basic and financial conditions are met and regulation 19 does not prevent it. The text of regulation 7 lists the subjects and does not itself say 'only if'; the three facts are the answers to the questions of this layer and to sections 4 and 5 of the Act.
@export Can I be entitled to Universal Credit at all (reg 7)?
GIVEN `I meet the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet all the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act (being at least the minimum age, under pension credit age, in Great Britain, not receiving education, and having accepted a claimant commitment, as the questions below explain)?
      `I meet the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act (your capital is within the limit, and the amount payable is not less than the minimum)?
      `regulation 19 prevents me from being entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 19 prevent you from being entitled (see the question on regulation 19)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be entitled to Universal Credit at all` IF
    `reg 7 — entitlement to universal credit can arise` `I meet the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act` `I meet the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act` `regulation 19 prevents me from being entitled`

§§ `Whether I can claim: my age and where I am (regulations 8 to 11)`

-- reg 8(4). A care leaver is a young person who was looked after by a local authority and is within the descriptions for England, Scotland or Wales.
@export Am I a care leaver (reg 8(4))?
GIVEN `the nation where I was looked after` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain were you looked after by a local authority (England, Wales or Scotland)?
      `I am an eligible child or a relevant child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In England: are you an eligible child (paragraph 19B of Schedule 2 to the Children Act 1989) or a relevant child (section 23A of that Act)?
      `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland: are you under 18?
      `a local authority looks after me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland: are you looked after by a local authority?
      `I am still owed advice and assistance or continuing care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland: have you stopped being looked after but are still owed advice and assistance under section 29(1) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995, or are you being given continuing care under section 26A of that Act?
      `I was looked after for 3 months or more since I was 14` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland: since you were 14, have you been looked after by a local authority for 3 months or more in total, not counting time placed with a member of your family?
      `I am a category 1 or category 2 young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Wales: are you a category 1 or category 2 young person within the meaning of section 104(2) of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a care leaver` IF
    `reg 8(4) — the person is a care leaver` `my care history`
    WHERE
        `my care history` MEANS `Young person who may be a care leaver` WITH
            `nation in which the care is provided` IS `the nation where I was looked after`
            `the person is an eligible child for the purposes of paragraph 19B of Schedule 2 to the Children Act 1989, or a relevant child for the purposes of section 23A of that Act` IS `I am an eligible child or a relevant child`
            `the person is under the age of 18` IS `I am under 18`
            `the person is looked after by a local authority` IS `a local authority looks after me`
            `the person has ceased to be looked after by a local authority but is a person to whom a local authority in Scotland is obliged to provide advice and assistance in terms of section 29(1) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995, or is being provided with continuing care under section 26A of that Act` IS `I am still owed advice and assistance or continuing care`
            `since reaching the age of 14 the person has been looked after by a local authority for a period of, or periods totalling, 3 months or more, excluding any period where the person has been placed with a member of their family` IS `I was looked after for 3 months or more since I was 14`
            `the person is a category 1 young person or category 2 young person within the meaning of section 104(2) of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` IS `I am a category 1 or category 2 young person`

-- reg 8(4). "Confinement" is labour resulting in the birth of a living child, or labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulting in the birth of a child, whether alive or dead.
@export Does my labour count as a confinement (reg 8(4))?
GIVEN `my labour resulted in the birth of a living child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your labour result in the birth of a living child?
      `my labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulted in the birth of a child, whether alive or dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy result in the birth of a child, whether alive or dead?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my labour count as a confinement` IF
    `reg 8(4) — a confinement` `my labour resulted in the birth of a living child` `my labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulted in the birth of a child, whether alive or dead`

-- reg 8(1)(f). The period runs from 11 weeks before the expected week of confinement to 15 weeks after the date of confinement.
@export Am I within the period around a pregnancy on a given day (reg 8(1)(f))?
GIVEN `I am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant?
      `the first day of my expected week of confinement` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week in which you expect to be confined? (Any date if you are not pregnant.)
      `I have been confined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been confined (given birth)?
      `the date of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you confined? (Any date if you have not been.)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I within the period around a pregnancy on a given day` IF
    `reg 8(1)(f) — pregnant or recently confined on a day` `my pregnancy` `the day I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `my pregnancy` MEANS `Pregnancy of a person` WITH
            `first day of the expected week of confinement, if the person is pregnant` IS IF `I am pregnant` THEN JUST `the first day of my expected week of confinement` ELSE NOTHING
            `date of confinement, if the person was pregnant and has been confined` IS IF `I have been confined` THEN JUST `the date of my confinement` ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 8(3). Without parental support: not looked after by a local authority and (a) no parent, (b) estranged from them or at serious risk living with them, or (c) living away from them where every parent is unable to support the person financially.
@export Am I without parental support (reg 8(3))?
GIVEN `I am looked after within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you looked after by a local authority within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989 (England)?
      `I am looked after within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you looked after by a local authority within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 (Scotland)?
      `I am looked after within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you looked after by a local authority within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 (Wales)?
      `I have no parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have no parent?
      `I am estranged from my parents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to live with your parents because you are estranged from them?
      `living with my parents would put me at serious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to live with your parents because there is a serious risk to your physical or mental health, or you would suffer significant harm?
      `I am living away from my parents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you living away from your parents?
      `every parent of mine is unable to support me financially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each of your parents unable to support you financially, because of a physical or mental impairment, because they are in custody (pending trial, or under a sentence), or because they are prohibited from entering Great Britain?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I without parental support` IF
    `reg 8(3) — the person is without parental support` `my situation`
    WHERE
        `my care` MEANS `Care of a child` WITH
            `looked after within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989` IS `I am looked after within the meaning of section 22 of the Children Act 1989`
            `looked after within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995` IS `I am looked after within the meaning of section 17(6) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995`
            `looked after within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` IS `I am looked after within the meaning of section 74 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`
        `a local authority looks after me` MEANS
            `reg 2 — looked after by a local authority` `my care`
        `my situation` MEANS `Young person who may be without parental support` WITH
            `the person is being looked after by a local authority` IS `a local authority looks after me`
            `the person has no parent` IS `I have no parent`
            `the person cannot live with their parents because the person is estranged from them` IS `I am estranged from my parents`
            `the person cannot live with their parents because there is a serious risk to the person's physical or mental health, or that the person would suffer significant harm if the person lived with them` IS `living with my parents would put me at serious risk`
            `the person is living away from their parents` IS `I am living away from my parents`
            `the person's parents` IS IF `every parent of mine is unable to support me financially` THEN LIST `a parent who is unable to support me` ELSE LIST `a parent who is able to support me`
        `a parent who is unable to support me` MEANS `Parent of a young person` WITH
            `the parent has a physical or mental impairment` IS TRUE  -- stand-in: the question asks only whether each parent is unable on one of the three grounds
            `the parent is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court` IS FALSE
            `the parent is prohibited from entering or re-entering Great Britain` IS FALSE
        `a parent who is able to support me` MEANS `Parent of a young person` WITH
            `the parent has a physical or mental impairment` IS FALSE  -- stand-in for a parent who is on none of the three grounds
            `the parent is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court` IS FALSE
            `the parent is prohibited from entering or re-entering Great Britain` IS FALSE

-- reg 8(1), (2). The minimum age is 18, but 16 for a person within one of the cases (a) to (g). Several of the facts below are the answers to other questions of this layer.
@export Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18 (reg 8(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been decided, on the assessment under Part 5 of the Regulations, that you have limited capability for work?
      `I am waiting for the assessment of my capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you waiting for that assessment to decide whether you have limited capability for work?
      `I have a fit note saying I am not fit for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a statement (a fit note) given in accordance with the Medical Evidence Regulations saying you are not fit for work?
      `I have regular and substantial caring responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person (see the question on regulation 30)?
      `I am responsible for a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you responsible for a child (see the question on regulation 4)?
      `my partner is responsible for a child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner responsible for a child or qualifying young person?
      `my partner meets the basic conditions in section 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your partner meet the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act?
      `I am within the period around a pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant and no more than 11 weeks before your expected week of confinement, or were you pregnant and no more than 15 weeks have passed since the date of your confinement (see the question on regulation 8(1)(f))?
      `I am without parental support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you without parental support (see the question on regulation 8(3))?
      `I am a care leaver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a care leaver (see the question on regulation 8(4))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the minimum age for me 16 rather than 18` IF
    `reg 8(1) — the minimum age is 16` `my circumstances`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS `Person who may have the minimum age of 16` WITH
            `the person has limited capability for work` IS `I have limited capability for work`
            `the person is awaiting an assessment under Part 5 to determine whether the person has limited capability for work` IS `I am waiting for the assessment of my capability for work`
            `the person has a statement given in accordance with the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work` IS `I have a fit note saying I am not fit for work`
            `the person has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` IS `I have regular and substantial caring responsibilities`
            `the person is responsible for a child` IS `I am responsible for a child`
            `the person is a member of a couple the other member of which is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person` IS `my partner is responsible for a child or qualifying young person`
            `the other member meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act` IS `my partner meets the basic conditions in section 4`
            `the person is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement` IS `I am within the period around a pregnancy`
            `the person is without parental support` IS `I am without parental support`
            `the person is a care leaver` IS `I am a care leaver`

@export What is the minimum age that applies to me (reg 8)?
GIVEN `the minimum age is 16 for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the minimum age for you 16 rather than 18 (see the previous question)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the minimum age that applies to me` IS
    `reg 8 — the minimum age` `the minimum age is 16 for me`

@export Do I meet the basic condition on age (reg 8)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
      `the minimum age is 16 for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the minimum age for you 16 rather than 18 (see the question on regulation 8(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the basic condition on age` IF
    `reg 8 — the person meets the basic condition on age` `my date of birth` `the day I am asking about` `the minimum age is 16 for me`

-- reg 9(2), (3), (3A). A right to reside counts unless it is of one of the kinds that paragraph (3) lists. Answer once for each right to reside you rely on; a yes to any one is enough.
@export Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit (reg 9(2), (3), (3A))?
GIVEN `my right comes from regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the right come from, or accord with, regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations?
      `my right under regulation 14 exists only because I am a jobseeker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the right come from regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because you are a qualified person as a jobseeker (regulation 6(1))?
      `my right under regulation 14 exists only because I am a family member of a jobseeker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the right come from regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because you are a family member of such a jobseeker?
      `my right under regulation 16 exists only because of regulation 16(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the right come from regulation 16 of the EEA Regulations only because you satisfy the criteria in regulation 16(5)?
      `I have limited leave under Appendix EU` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of Appendix EU to the immigration rules?
      `I have limited leave as a person with a Zambrano right to reside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted limited leave by virtue of being a person with a Zambrano right to reside, as defined in Annex 1 of Appendix EU?
      `I have limited leave after arriving with an Appendix EU (Family Permit) entry clearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted limited leave by virtue of arriving in the United Kingdom with an entry clearance granted under Appendix EU (Family Permit)?
      `my right was granted as a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the right granted by virtue of your being a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland?
      `I would have a right under the EEA Regulations if that person were an EEA national` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have a right to reside under the EEA Regulations if the relevant person of Northern Ireland were an EEA national?
      `that right would be one of the first four kinds above` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that right to reside be one of the kinds in paragraph (3)(a) or (b), that is, the first four kinds in the list above?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit` IF
    `reg 9(2) — the person has a right to reside that counts` (LIST `the right I rely on`)
    WHERE
        `the right I rely on` MEANS `Right to reside` WITH
            `the right exists by virtue of, or in accordance with, regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations` IS `my right comes from regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations`
            `the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6(1) of those Regulations as a jobseeker` IS `my right under regulation 14 exists only because I am a jobseeker`
            `the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a family member of such a jobseeker` IS `my right under regulation 14 exists only because I am a family member of a jobseeker`
            `the right exists under regulation 16 of the EEA Regulations only because the person satisfies the criteria in regulation 16(5) of those Regulations` IS `my right under regulation 16 exists only because of regulation 16(5)`
            `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of Appendix EU to the immigration rules` IS `I have limited leave under Appendix EU`
            `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of being a person with a Zambrano right to reside as defined in Annex 1 of Appendix EU` IS `I have limited leave as a person with a Zambrano right to reside`
            `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of having arrived in the United Kingdom with an entry clearance that was granted under Appendix EU (Family Permit)` IS `I have limited leave after arriving with an Appendix EU (Family Permit) entry clearance`
            `the right was granted by virtue of being a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland` IS `my right was granted as a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland`
            `the person would have a right to reside under the EEA Regulations if the relevant person of Northern Ireland were an EEA national` IS `I would have a right under the EEA Regulations if that person were an EEA national`
            `that right to reside would fall within paragraph (3)(a) or (b)` IS `that right would be one of the first four kinds above`

-- reg 9(4)(a) to (g). A person within one of these groups is not treated as outside Great Britain.
@export Am I within one of the groups in reg 9(4)(a) to (g) (workers, refugees and others)?
GIVEN `I am a worker or self-employed person under regulation 6 of the EEA Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6 of the EEA Regulations as a worker or a self-employed person?
      `I am a family member of such a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a family member of a person referred to in the previous question?
      `I have a permanent right to reside under regulation 15 of the EEA Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right to reside permanently in the United Kingdom by virtue of regulation 15(1)(c), (d) or (e) of the EEA Regulations?
      `I am a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland with a right within paragraph (3)(c)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland, with a right to reside which falls within paragraph (3)(c)(i) (limited leave under Appendix EU)?
      `that person is within paragraph (4)(a) or would be but for not being an EEA national` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that relevant person of Northern Ireland within the first question of this list (a worker or self-employed person), or would they be but for not being an EEA national?
      `I am a frontier worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a frontier worker within the meaning of regulation 3 of the Citizens' Rights (Frontier Workers) (EU Exit) Regulations 2020?
      `I am a family member of a frontier worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a family member of a frontier worker?
      `I have limited leave under Appendix EU as such a family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted limited leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom by virtue of Appendix EU?
      `I am a refugee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a refugee within Article 1 of the Convention relating to the Status of Refugees (Geneva, 28 July 1951) as extended by the 1967 Protocol?
      `I have humanitarian protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have humanitarian protection granted under the immigration rules?
      `I am in the United Kingdom after being deported, expelled or removed from another country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in the United Kingdom as a result of your deportation, expulsion or other removal by compulsion of law from another country, and not a person subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` IF
    `reg 9(4)(a) to (g) — the person is within one of the remaining limbs` `my status`
    WHERE
        `my status` MEANS `Person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)` WITH
            `the person is a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6 of the EEA Regulations as a worker or a self-employed person` IS `I am a worker or self-employed person under regulation 6 of the EEA Regulations`
            `the person is a family member of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (a)` IS `I am a family member of such a worker`
            `the person has a right to reside permanently in the United Kingdom by virtue of regulation 15(1)(c), (d) or (e) of the EEA Regulations` IS `I have a permanent right to reside under regulation 15 of the EEA Regulations`
            `the person is a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland, with a right to reside which falls within paragraph (3)(c)(i)` IS `I am a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland with a right within paragraph (3)(c)(i)`
            `the relevant person of Northern Ireland falls within paragraph (4)(a), or would do so but for the fact that they are not an EEA national` IS `that person is within paragraph (4)(a) or would be but for not being an EEA national`
            `the person is a frontier worker within the meaning of regulation 3 of the Citizens' Rights (Frontier Workers) (EU Exit) Regulations 2020` IS `I am a frontier worker`
            `the person is a family member of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (cb)` IS `I am a family member of a frontier worker`
            `the person has been granted limited leave to enter, or remain in, the United Kingdom by virtue of Appendix EU to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I have limited leave under Appendix EU as such a family member`
            `the person is a refugee within the definition in Article 1 of the Convention relating to the Status of Refugees done at Geneva on 28th July 1951, as extended by Article 1(2) of the Protocol relating to the Status of Refugees done at New York on 31st January 1967` IS `I am a refugee`
            `the person has humanitarian protection granted under the immigration rules` IS `I have humanitarian protection`
            `the person is not a person subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 and is in the United Kingdom as a result of their deportation, expulsion or other removal by compulsion of law from another country to the United Kingdom` IS `I am in the United Kingdom after being deported, expelled or removed from another country`

-- reg 9(4)(za) to (ze). Persons with leave under the Afghan schemes, and persons who left Afghanistan, Ukraine, Sudan or Israel and the region, with the leave or status the paragraph requires.
@export Am I within reg 9(4)(za) to (ze) (Afghan, Ukrainian, Sudanese or Israel and region schemes)?
GIVEN `I have leave under the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted leave under the immigration rules by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy?
      `I have leave under the Afghan ex-gratia scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted leave under the immigration rules by virtue of the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan (the ex-gratia scheme)?
      `I am in Great Britain and left Afghanistan when its government collapsed on 15 August 2021` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Great Britain, having left Afghanistan in connection with the collapse of the Afghan government on 15 August 2021?
      `I left Ukraine because of the Russian invasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you residing in Ukraine immediately before 1 January 2022 and did you leave in connection with the Russian invasion of 24 February 2022?
      `I left Sudan because of the violence from 15 April 2023` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you residing in Sudan before 15 April 2023 and did you leave in connection with the violence that escalated on that day in Khartoum and across Sudan?
      `I left Israel or the region because of the attack of 7 October 2023` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you residing in Israel, the West Bank, the Gaza Strip, East Jerusalem, the Golan Heights or Lebanon immediately before 7 October 2023 and did you leave in connection with the Hamas attack on that day or the violence that followed?
      `I have been granted leave under the immigration rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted leave under the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971?
      `I have a right of abode in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right of abode in the United Kingdom (section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971)?
      `I do not need leave to enter or remain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you not need leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom (section 3ZA of the Immigration Act 1971)?
      `I have been granted, or am deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted, or are you deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` IF
    `reg 9(4)(za) — leave by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy or the ex-gratia scheme` `my status`
    OR `reg 9(4)(zb) — a person who left Afghanistan on the collapse of its government` `my status` (`reg 9(4)(e) — a person who has been granted, or is deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules` `my status`)
    OR `reg 9(4)(zc) — a person who left Ukraine` `my status`
    OR `reg 9(4)(zd) — a person who left Sudan` `my status`
    OR `reg 9(4)(ze) — a person who left Israel or the region` `my status`
    WHERE
        `my status` MEANS `Person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` WITH
            `the person has been granted leave in accordance with the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy` IS `I have leave under the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy`
            `the person has been granted leave in accordance with the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan (the ex-gratia scheme)` IS `I have leave under the Afghan ex-gratia scheme`
            `the person is in Great Britain and left Afghanistan in connection with the collapse of the Afghan government that took place on 15th August 2021` IS `I am in Great Britain and left Afghanistan when its government collapsed on 15 August 2021`
            `the person was residing in Ukraine immediately before 1st January 2022 and left Ukraine in connection with the Russian invasion which took place on 24th February 2022` IS `I left Ukraine because of the Russian invasion`
            `the person was residing in Sudan before 15th April 2023 and left Sudan in connection with the violence which rapidly escalated on 15th April 2023 in Khartoum and across Sudan` IS `I left Sudan because of the violence from 15 April 2023`
            `the person was residing in Israel, the West Bank, the Gaza Strip, East Jerusalem, the Golan Heights or Lebanon immediately before 7th October 2023 and left in connection with the Hamas terrorist attack in Israel on 7th October 2023 or the violence which rapidly escalated in the region following the attack` IS `I left Israel or the region because of the attack of 7 October 2023`
            `the person has been granted leave in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I have been granted leave under the immigration rules`
            `the person has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I have a right of abode in the United Kingdom`
            `the person does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I do not need leave to enter or remain`
            `the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it, or arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person has left that country or territory and is present in Great Britain` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person has leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person, as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route, has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 or leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person has been granted, or is deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I have been granted, or am deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules`

-- reg 9(4)(e), (zf), (zg), (4A). Leave outside the rules; a person who left a country from which British nationals were advised to leave or evacuated (for 6 months from the advice or evacuation); and a safe and legal humanitarian route.
@export Am I within reg 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg) (leave outside the rules, evacuees, humanitarian routes)?
GIVEN `the day the Government advised British nationals to leave, or the evacuation began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Government issue the public information advising British nationals to leave that country, or the evacuation begin?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
      `I have been granted leave under the immigration rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted leave under the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971?
      `I have a right of abode in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right of abode in the United Kingdom (section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971)?
      `I do not need leave to enter or remain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you not need leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom (section 3ZA of the Immigration Act 1971)?
      `I was living in a country when British nationals were advised to leave it or were evacuated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you living in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before the Government advised British nationals to leave it, or arranged their evacuation?
      `I have left that country and am in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you left that country or territory and are you now in Great Britain?
      `I have leave on a discretionary basis outside the immigration rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave on a discretionary basis outside the rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971?
      `I have leave on a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have leave to enter or remain, as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route, under the immigration rules or on a discretionary basis outside them?
      `I have been granted, or am deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted, or are you deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)` IF
    (`reg 9(4)(zf) — a person who left a country from which British nationals were advised to leave or evacuated` `my status`
     AND `reg 9(4A) — the day is within the 6 months for a person within paragraph (4)(zf)` `the day the Government advised British nationals to leave, or the evacuation began` `the day I am asking about`)
    OR `reg 9(4)(zg) — a person with leave on a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route` `my status`
    OR `reg 9(4)(e) — a person who has been granted, or is deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules` `my status`
    WHERE
        `my status` MEANS `Person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)` WITH
            `the person has been granted leave in accordance with the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person has been granted leave in accordance with the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan (the ex-gratia scheme)` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person is in Great Britain and left Afghanistan in connection with the collapse of the Afghan government that took place on 15th August 2021` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person was residing in Ukraine immediately before 1st January 2022 and left Ukraine in connection with the Russian invasion which took place on 24th February 2022` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person was residing in Sudan before 15th April 2023 and left Sudan in connection with the violence which rapidly escalated on 15th April 2023 in Khartoum and across Sudan` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person was residing in Israel, the West Bank, the Gaza Strip, East Jerusalem, the Golan Heights or Lebanon immediately before 7th October 2023 and left in connection with the Hamas terrorist attack in Israel on 7th October 2023 or the violence which rapidly escalated in the region following the attack` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the person has been granted leave in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I have been granted leave under the immigration rules`
            `the person has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I have a right of abode in the United Kingdom`
            `the person does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I do not need leave to enter or remain`
            `the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it, or arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it` IS `I was living in a country when British nationals were advised to leave it or were evacuated`
            `the person has left that country or territory and is present in Great Britain` IS `I have left that country and am in Great Britain`
            `the person has leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I have leave on a discretionary basis outside the immigration rules`
            `the person, as part of a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route, has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 or leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules` IS `I have leave on a safe and legal humanitarian immigration route`
            `the person has been granted, or is deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971` IS `I have been granted, or am deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules`

-- reg 9(1). A person is treated as not in Great Britain if not habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man or the Republic of Ireland (and, under paragraph (2), a habitual residence needs a right to reside that counts), unless within paragraph (4). The last three facts are the answers to the questions above.
-- Paragraph (4) is a list of alternatives, so each group's combined answer is passed in one slot of the module rule and the other slots of that group are left false.
@export Am I treated as not being in Great Britain, so that I cannot claim (reg 9(1))?
GIVEN `I am habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man or the Republic of Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man or the Republic of Ireland?
      `I have a right to reside that counts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Do I have a right to reside that counts for Universal Credit" give the answer yes?
      `I am within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Am I within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)" give the answer yes?
      `I am within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Am I within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)" give the answer yes?
      `I am within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Am I within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)" give the answer yes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as not being in Great Britain` IF
    `reg 9(1) — the person is treated as not being in Great Britain` `I am habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man or the Republic of Ireland` `I have a right to reside that counts` `within paragraph (4)`
    WHERE
        `within paragraph (4)` MEANS
            `reg 9(4) — the person falls within this paragraph`
                `I am within regulation 9(4)(za) to (ze)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `I am within regulation 9(4)(e), (zf) or (zg)` FALSE FALSE `I am within one of the groups in regulation 9(4)(a) to (g)`

-- reg 10(1). The question is answered 'yes' when the person does NOT have to meet the condition of being in Great Britain.
@export Do I have to be in Great Britain to claim, as a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas, or as their partner (reg 10)?
GIVEN `I hold an office or employment under the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office or employment under the Crown?
      `I am a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of Her Majesty's forces (within the Armed Forces Act 2006)?
      `I am performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of the forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces?
      `I was habitually resident in the United Kingdom before my posting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you habitually resident in the United Kingdom immediately before your posting (or the first of consecutive postings)?
      `we are joint claimants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming jointly with your partner?
      `my partner is posted overseas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas?
      `I am accompanying my partner on that posting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you accompanying your partner on that posting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have to be in Great Britain to claim, as a Crown servant or member of the forces posted overseas, or as their partner` IF
    `reg 10(1) — the person does not have to meet the basic condition to be in Great Britain` (`reg 10(1)(a) — a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces posted overseas` `my posting`) `we are joint claimants` `my partner is posted overseas` `I am accompanying my partner on that posting`
    WHERE
        `my posting` MEANS `Person who may be posted overseas` WITH
            `the person holds an office or employment under the Crown` IS `I hold an office or employment under the Crown`
            `the person is a member of Her Majesty's forces within the meaning of the Armed Forces Act 2006` IS `I am a member of Her Majesty's forces`
            `the person is performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces` IS `I am performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of the forces`
            `the person was, immediately before their posting or the first of consecutive postings, habitually resident in the United Kingdom` IS `I was habitually resident in the United Kingdom before my posting`

-- reg 11(2). 1 month, or up to 2 months where the absence is in connection with a death and it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return within the first month.
@export How many months of absence from Great Britain can be disregarded after a death (reg 11(2))?
GIVEN `the absence is in connection with the death of my partner or of a child or qualifying young person I was responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence in connection with the death of your partner, or of a child or qualifying young person you were responsible for?
      `the absence is in connection with the death of a close relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence in connection with the death of a close relative of yours, or of your partner, or of a child or qualifying young person you or your partner were responsible for?
      `the Secretary of State considers it unreasonable to expect me to return within the first month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State decided that it would be unreasonable to expect you to return to Great Britain within the first month?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months of absence from Great Britain can be disregarded after a death` IS
    `reg 11(2) — the months of absence that may be disregarded` `the absence is in connection with the death of my partner or of a child or qualifying young person I was responsible for` `the absence is in connection with the death of a close relative` `the Secretary of State considers it unreasonable to expect me to return within the first month`

@export Does regulation 11(4A) apply to me because I was abroad when British nationals were advised to leave (reg 11(4A))?
GIVEN `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government advised British nationals to leave it, or evacuated them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before the Government advised British nationals to leave it, or arranged their evacuation?
      `paragraphs (1)(a), (1)(b)(i), (1)(b)(ii) or (2) applied to me then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did regulation 11(1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (2) apply to you when the advice was issued or the evacuation began?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is unreasonable to expect me to return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect you to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain?
      `I did not go into that country when the advice was to leave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not enter that country or territory when the Government's advice was to leave it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 11(4A) apply to me because I was abroad when British nationals were advised to leave` IF
    `reg 11(4A) — paragraph (4A) applies` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `Person who may be within regulation 11(4A)` WITH
            `the person was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it, or arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it` IS `I was in a country outside Great Britain when the Government advised British nationals to leave it, or evacuated them`
            `paragraphs (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (2) applied to the person when the public information was issued or the evacuation began` IS `paragraphs (1)(a), (1)(b)(i), (1)(b)(ii) or (2) applied to me then`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is unreasonable to expect me to return`
            `the person did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it` IS `I did not go into that country when the advice was to leave it`

-- reg 11. A temporary absence is disregarded if you were entitled to Universal Credit immediately before it began and it is not expected to exceed, and does not exceed, one month (extended by up to a further month by paragraph (2)), or paragraph (3) or (4) applies (absences of no more than 6 months for treatment, or of a mariner or continental shelf worker), or paragraph (4A) applies; the total disregarded never exceeds 6 months (paragraph (4B)).
-- The last fact is the answer to the question on regulation 11(4A).
@export Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded, so that I can keep my entitlement (reg 11)?
GIVEN `the day my absence began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your absence from Great Britain begin?
      `the day to which my absence has lasted` IS A DATE @desc Up to what day has the absence lasted so far (today, if it is still going on)?
      `the day my absence is expected to end` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the absence expected to end?
      `I was entitled to universal credit immediately before the absence began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to Universal Credit immediately before the absence began?
      `the absence is in connection with the death of my partner or of a child or qualifying young person I was responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence in connection with the death of your partner, or of a child or qualifying young person you were responsible for?
      `the absence is in connection with the death of a close relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence in connection with the death of a close relative of yours, or of your partner, or of a child or qualifying young person you or your partner were responsible for?
      `the Secretary of State considers it unreasonable to expect me to return within the first month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State decided that it would be unreasonable to expect you to return to Great Britain within the first month?
      `regulation 11(4A) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Does regulation 11(4A) apply to me because I was abroad when British nationals were advised to leave" give the answer yes?
      `my absence is solely for treatment of an illness or impairment by or under a qualified practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence solely in connection with your undergoing treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment by, or under the supervision of, a qualified practitioner?
      `my absence is solely for medically approved convalescence or care for an illness I had before leaving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence solely in connection with medically approved convalescence or care as a result of treatment, for an illness or impairment you had before leaving Great Britain?
      `my absence is solely to accompany my partner or a child for treatment or convalescence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence solely in connection with accompanying your partner, or a child or qualifying young person you are responsible for, for treatment, convalescence or care of those kinds?
      `I am a mariner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a mariner?
      `I am a continental shelf worker in a designated or prescribed area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a continental shelf worker who is in a designated area or a prescribed area?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded` IF
    `reg 11 — the temporary absence is disregarded` `my absence` `I was entitled to universal credit immediately before the absence began` (`reg 11(2) — the months of absence that may be disregarded` `the absence is in connection with the death of my partner or of a child or qualifying young person I was responsible for` `the absence is in connection with the death of a close relative` `the Secretary of State considers it unreasonable to expect me to return within the first month`) (`reg 11(3) — paragraph (3) applies` `my absence` `my reason`) (`reg 11(4) — paragraph (4) applies` `my absence` `my reason`) `regulation 11(4A) applies to me`
    WHERE
        `my absence` MEANS `Absence that is measured against a limit` WITH
            `first day of the absence` IS `the day my absence began`
            `day to which the absence has lasted` IS `the day to which my absence has lasted`
            `expected last day of the absence` IS `the day my absence is expected to end`
        `my reason` MEANS `Reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` WITH
            `the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment by, or under the supervision of, a qualified practitioner` IS `my absence is solely for treatment of an illness or impairment by or under a qualified practitioner`
            `the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing medically approved convalescence or care as a result of treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment, where the person had that illness or impairment before leaving Great Britain` IS `my absence is solely for medically approved convalescence or care for an illness I had before leaving`
            `the absence is solely in connection with the person accompanying their partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom they are responsible for treatment or convalescence or care as mentioned in sub-paragraph (a)` IS `my absence is solely to accompany my partner or a child for treatment or convalescence`
            `the person is a mariner` IS `I am a mariner`
            `the person is a continental shelf worker who is in a designated area or a prescribed area` IS `I am a continental shelf worker in a designated or prescribed area`

§§ `Whether I can claim: education and my claimant commitment (regulations 12 to 16)`

-- reg 12(1B). A traineeship is a course funded by the Secretary of State or the Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding, lasting no more than 6 months, with training and a work experience placement, open to people who are 16 but not yet 25 on its first day.
@export Am I on a traineeship (reg 12(1B))?
GIVEN `the course is funded by the Secretary of State or the Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the course funded, in whole or in part, by (or under arrangements made by) the Secretary of State under section 14 of the Education Act 2002, or the Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding?
      `the first day of the course` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the course start?
      `the last day of the course` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the course end?
      `the course includes training and a work experience placement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the course include training to help prepare you for work and a work experience placement?
      `the course is open to people aged 16 but not 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the course open to people who, on its first day, have reached 16 but not 25?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I on a traineeship` IF
    `reg 12(1B) — the course is a traineeship` `my course`
    WHERE
        `my course` MEANS `Course that may be a traineeship` WITH
            `the course is funded in whole or in part by, or under arrangements made by, the Secretary of State under section 14 of the Education Act 2002 or the Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding` IS `the course is funded by the Secretary of State or the Chief Executive of Education and Skills Funding`
            `first day of the course` IS `the first day of the course`
            `last day of the course` IS `the last day of the course`
            `the course includes training to help prepare the participant for work and a work experience placement` IS `the course includes training and a work experience placement`
            `the course is open to persons who on the first day of the course have reached the age of 16 but not 25` IS `the course is open to people aged 16 but not 25`

-- reg 12(1B). A relevant training scheme is a traineeship, or a course or scheme of training for work that you attend as a work preparation requirement or voluntarily and to which the Secretary of State referred you.
@export Am I taking part in a relevant training scheme (reg 12(1B))?
GIVEN `my course is a traineeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your course a traineeship (see the previous question)?
      `the course or scheme is education or training to gain the skills needed for paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the course or scheme comprise education or training designed to help you gain the skills needed to obtain paid work, or more or better-paid work?
      `I attend it as a work preparation requirement or as voluntary work preparation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend it because of a work preparation requirement (section 22 of the Act), or as voluntary work preparation?
      `the Secretary of State referred me to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State refer you to the course or scheme?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taking part in a relevant training scheme` IF
    `reg 12(1B) — the person is participating in a relevant training scheme` `my course is a traineeship` `the course or scheme is education or training to gain the skills needed for paid work` `I attend it as a work preparation requirement or as voluntary work preparation` `the Secretary of State referred me to it`

@export Is my course a course of advanced education (reg 12(3))?
GIVEN `the course leads to a postgraduate degree or comparable qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the course lead to a postgraduate degree or comparable qualification?
      `the course leads to a first degree or comparable qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it lead to a first degree or comparable qualification?
      `the course leads to a diploma of higher education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it lead to a diploma of higher education?
      `the course leads to a higher national diploma` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it lead to a higher national diploma?
      `the course is of a standard above advanced GNVQ, A level or Scottish Higher or Advanced Higher` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it any other course of study of a standard above advanced GNVQ or equivalent (including above A level, or a Scottish Higher or Advanced Higher)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my course a course of advanced education` IF
    `reg 12(3) — the course is a course of advanced education` `my course`
    WHERE
        `my course` MEANS `Course that may be a course of advanced education` WITH
            `the course leads to a postgraduate degree or comparable qualification` IS `the course leads to a postgraduate degree or comparable qualification`
            `the course leads to a first degree or comparable qualification` IS `the course leads to a first degree or comparable qualification`
            `the course leads to a diploma of higher education` IS `the course leads to a diploma of higher education`
            `the course leads to a higher national diploma` IS `the course leads to a higher national diploma`
            `the course is of a standard above advanced GNVQ or equivalent, including above a general certificate of education (advanced level) or above a Scottish national qualification (higher or advanced higher)` IS `the course is of a standard above advanced GNVQ, A level or Scottish Higher or Advanced Higher`

-- reg 12. A qualifying young person is treated as receiving education unless in a relevant training scheme. Otherwise: a full-time course of advanced education, or another full-time course at an educational establishment for which a student loan or grant is provided for maintenance; or a course not compatible with any work-related requirement. Two facts are the answers to other questions.
@export Am I receiving education, so that I cannot claim (reg 12)?
GIVEN `I am a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a qualifying young person (see the question on regulation 5)?
      `I am taking part in a relevant training scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Am I taking part in a relevant training scheme" give the answer yes?
      `I am on a full-time course of advanced education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undertaking a full-time course of advanced education (see the question on regulation 12(3))?
      `I am on another full-time course for which I get a student loan or grant for maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undertaking any other full-time course of study or training at an educational establishment for which a student loan or grant is provided for your maintenance?
      `my course is not compatible with any work-related requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undertaking a course of study or training that is not compatible with any work-related requirement the Secretary of State imposes on you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I receiving education` IF
    `reg 12 — the person is receiving education` `I am a qualifying young person` `I am taking part in a relevant training scheme` `I am on a full-time course of advanced education` `I am on another full-time course for which I get a student loan or grant for maintenance` `my course is not compatible with any work-related requirement`

-- reg 13. A person undertakes a course from the day they start it (or the part of a modular course) to its last day (or an earlier day of finally abandoning it or being dismissed from it), including, for a modular course, time retaking or completing a module and vacations, but not a vacation straight after the final module; and not on a day when paragraph (4) applies.
-- The last fact is the answer to the question on regulation 13(4).
@export Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day (reg 13(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `my course is modular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the course a modular course (two or more modules, a specified number of which must be completed)?
      `the day I started the course or the part` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you start the course (or, for a modular course, the part you are asking about)?
      `the last day of the course or part` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the course (or, for a part of a modular course, the last day you are registered to undertake that part)?
      `I have finally abandoned the course or been dismissed from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you finally abandoned the course, or been dismissed from it?
      `the day I abandoned it or was dismissed` IS A DATE @desc On what day? (Any date if you have not.)
      `I retake examinations or complete a module after failing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a modular course: do you undertake the course for a period to retake examinations or complete a module after failing it?
      `the first day of that period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does that period begin? (Any date if there is none.)
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does that period end? (Any date if there is none.)
      `I have a vacation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a modular course: do you have a vacation within the course, or straight after it?
      `the first day of the vacation` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the vacation begin? (Any date if there is none.)
      `the last day of the vacation` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the vacation end? (Any date if there is none.)
      `the vacation comes straight after the last day of my final registered module` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the vacation come straight after the last day on which you are to attend or undertake the final module you registered for?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
      `regulation 13(4) applies to me on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question "Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring" give the answer yes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I regarded as undertaking my course on a given day` IF
    `reg 13 — the person is regarded as undertaking the course on the day`
        (`reg 13(1) — the day falls within the period of the course or part` `my course` `the day I am asking about`)
        (`reg 13(2)(a) — the day falls within a period of retaking or completing` `my course` `the day I am asking about`)
        (`reg 13(2)(b) — the day falls within a vacation that the period includes` `my course` `the day I am asking about`)
        `regulation 13(4) applies to me on that day`
    WHERE
        `my course` MEANS `Course that a person may be undertaking` WITH
            `the course is a modular course` IS `my course is modular`
            `day on which the person starts undertaking the course, or the part of the modular course` IS `the day I started the course or the part`
            `last day of the course or, for a part of a modular course, last day on which the person is registered as undertaking that part` IS `the last day of the course or part`
            `day on which the person finally abandons the course or is dismissed from it` IS IF `I have finally abandoned the course or been dismissed from it` THEN JUST `the day I abandoned it or was dismissed` ELSE NOTHING
            `periods in which the person undertakes the course to retake examinations or to complete a module after failing` IS IF `I retake examinations or complete a module after failing` THEN LIST `my period of retaking` ELSE EMPTY
            `vacations` IS IF `I have a vacation` THEN LIST `my vacation` ELSE EMPTY
        `my period of retaking` MEANS `Period of days` WITH
            `first day` IS `the first day of that period`
            `last day` IS `the last day of that period`
        `my vacation` MEANS `Vacation during a course` WITH
            `period of the vacation` IS `the period of my vacation`
            `the vacation is immediately after the last day on which the person is to attend or undertake the final module in the course that the person has registered to attend or undertake` IS `the vacation comes straight after the last day of my final registered module`
        `the period of my vacation` MEANS `Period of days` WITH
            `first day` IS `the first day of the vacation`
            `last day` IS `the last day of the vacation`

-- reg 13(4). Not regarded as undertaking a course while: you have, with the educational establishment's consent, stopped attending because you are ill or caring for someone; you have recovered, or stopped caring, within the past year but not yet resumed; and you are not eligible for a grant or student loan.
@export Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring (reg 13(4))?
GIVEN `I stopped attending with the establishment's consent because I was ill or caring for another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, with the consent of the educational establishment, stopped attending or undertaking the course because you are ill or caring for another person?
      `I have recovered or stopped caring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you recovered from the illness, or stopped caring for that person?
      `the day I recovered or stopped caring` IS A DATE @desc On what day? (Any date if you have not.)
      `I have resumed the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you resumed the course?
      `the day I resumed the course` IS A DATE @desc On what day? (Any date if you have not.)
      `I am eligible for a grant or student loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for a grant or a student loan?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not regarded as undertaking my course because I stopped for illness or caring` IF
    `reg 13(4) — the person is not regarded as undertaking the course on the day` `my interruption` `the day I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `my interruption` MEANS `Interruption of a course` WITH
            `the person has, with the consent of the relevant educational establishment, ceased to attend or undertake the course because they are ill or caring for another person` IS `I stopped attending with the establishment's consent because I was ill or caring for another person`
            `day on which the person recovered from that illness or ceased caring for that person` IS IF `I have recovered or stopped caring` THEN JUST `the day I recovered or stopped caring` ELSE NOTHING
            `day on which the person resumed the course` IS IF `I have resumed the course` THEN JUST `the day I resumed the course` ELSE NOTHING
            `the person is eligible for a grant or student loan` IS `I am eligible for a grant or student loan`

@export Am I excepted from the education condition because I am on a full-time course, under 21 and without parental support (reg 14(1)(a))?
GIVEN `I am undertaking a full-time course that is not a course of advanced education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undertaking a full-time course of study or training that is not a course of advanced education?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
      `I reached 21 while undertaking the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are 21: did you reach 21 while undertaking the course?
      `I am without parental support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you without parental support (see the question on regulation 8(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excepted from the education condition because I am on a full-time course, under 21 and without parental support` IF
    `reg 14(1)(a) — the person is on a full-time course, under 21, without parental support` `I am undertaking a full-time course that is not a course of advanced education` `my date of birth` `the day I am asking about` `I reached 21 while undertaking the course` `I am without parental support`

-- reg 14(1)(b). Entitled to attendance allowance, pension age disability payment, disability living allowance, Scottish adult disability living allowance, child disability payment, adult disability payment or personal independence payment, and found (or treated) to have limited capability for work before starting education.
@export Am I excepted from the education condition because I get a disability benefit and was found to have limited capability for work (reg 14(1)(b))?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to one of the benefits that regulation 14(1)(b) lists (attendance allowance, pension age disability payment, disability living allowance, Scottish adult disability living allowance, child disability payment, adult disability payment, personal independence payment)?
      `the benefit I am entitled to` IS A Benefit @desc Which of those benefits are you entitled to? (If more than one, choose any one.)
      `before I started receiving education I was found to have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before you started receiving education, was it determined, on an assessment under Part 5 of the Regulations (or Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations), that you have limited capability for work or limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `before I started receiving education I was treated as having limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before you started receiving education, were you treated as having limited capability for work under Schedule 8, or for work and work-related activity under Schedule 9?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excepted from the education condition because I get a disability benefit and was found to have limited capability for work` IF
    `reg 14(1)(b) — the person is entitled to a disability benefit and was found to have limited capability for work` (IF `I am entitled to a benefit` THEN LIST `the benefit I am entitled to` ELSE EMPTY) `before I started receiving education I was found to have limited capability for work` `before I started receiving education I was treated as having limited capability for work`

@export Am I excepted from the education condition because my partner and I are both in education and my partner looks after a child (reg 14(1)(e))?
GIVEN `my partner and I are both receiving education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and your partner both receiving education?
      `my partner is responsible for a child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner responsible for a child or qualifying young person?
      `the nation of Great Britain where the child is placed with my partner` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the child placed with my partner (England, Wales or Scotland)?
      `the child is placed with my partner under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child placed with my partner under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (England) Regulations 2010, the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (Wales) Regulations 2015, or the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009 (whichever applies in that nation)?
      `my partner is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland: is your partner a foster carer or a kinship carer with whom the child is placed? (Any answer elsewhere.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excepted from the education condition because my partner and I are both in education and my partner looks after a child` IF
    `reg 14(1)(e) — both members of the couple are receiving education and the other is responsible for a child or is a foster parent` `my partner and I are both receiving education` `my partner is responsible for a child or qualifying young person` `my partner is a foster parent with a child placed`
    WHERE
        `my partner's placement` MEANS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
            `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation of Great Britain where the child is placed with my partner`
            `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `the child is placed with my partner under the placement regulations`
            `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `my partner is a foster carer or a kinship carer`
        `my partner is a foster parent with a child placed` MEANS
            `reg 2 — foster parent` `my partner's placement`

-- reg 14(1). Excepted if any of (a) to (f) applies. The first, second and fifth facts are the answers to the three questions above on regulation 14(1)(a), (b) and (e).
@export Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education (reg 14(1))?
GIVEN `I am within regulation 14(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 14(1)(a) (full-time course, under 21, without parental support) give the answer yes?
      `I am within regulation 14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 14(1)(b) (disability benefit and limited capability for work) give the answer yes?
      `I am responsible for a child or a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you responsible for a child or a qualifying young person (see the question on regulation 4)?
      `I am a single person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a single person (not a member of a couple)?
      `the nation of Great Britain where the child is placed with me` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the child placed with me (England, Wales or Scotland)?
      `the child is placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child placed with me under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (England) Regulations 2010, the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review (Wales) Regulations 2015, or the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009 (whichever applies in that nation)?
      `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland: are you a foster carer or a kinship carer with whom the child is placed? (Any answer elsewhere.)
      `I am within regulation 14(1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 14(1)(e) (both of a couple in education) give the answer yes?
      `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the qualifying age for state pension credit?
      `my partner has not reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner a member of the couple who has not reached that age?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excepted from the condition of not receiving education` IF
    `reg 14(1) — the person is excepted from the basic condition in section 4(1)(d)` `I am within regulation 14(1)(a)` `I am within regulation 14(1)(b)` `I am responsible for a child or a qualifying young person` `I am a single person and a foster parent with a child placed` `I am within regulation 14(1)(e)` `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` `my partner has not reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`
    WHERE
        `my placement` MEANS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
            `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation of Great Britain where the child is placed with me`
            `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `the child is placed with me under the placement regulations`
            `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer`
        `I am a foster parent with a child placed` MEANS
            `reg 2 — foster parent` `my placement`
        `I am a single person and a foster parent with a child placed` MEANS
            (`I am a single person`) AND (`I am a foster parent with a child placed`)

-- reg 15(1), (3). If you accept a claimant commitment within the period the Secretary of State specifies after you claim (or any longer period the Secretary of State allows on your request for a review of a work search or work availability requirement or of a limitation), it is treated as accepted on the first day of the period for which you claim. Otherwise the answer is NOTHING.
@export On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted (reg 15(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the first day of the period for which I claim` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period for which you are claiming?
      `I have accepted a claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you accepted a claimant commitment?
      `the day I accepted it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you accept it? (Any date if you have not.)
      `the last day of the period the Secretary of State specified` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period the Secretary of State specified for accepting a claimant commitment?
      `the Secretary of State extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State extended that period because you asked for a review of a work search or work availability requirement, or of a limitation, and found the request reasonable?
      `the last day of the extended period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the extended period? (Any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted` IS
    `reg 15(1) — the day on which the claimant commitment is treated as accepted` `the first day of the period for which I claim` (IF `I have accepted a claimant commitment` THEN JUST `the day I accepted it` ELSE NOTHING) `the last day of the period the Secretary of State specified` (IF `the Secretary of State extended the period` THEN JUST `the last day of the extended period` ELSE NOTHING)

@export On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted where my award is made without a claim (reg 15(2))?
GIVEN `the day that would be the first day of my first assessment period` IS A DATE @desc What would be the first day of your first assessment period (see the question on regulation 21(3) or (3A))?
      `I have accepted a claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you accepted a claimant commitment?
      `the day I accepted it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you accept it? (Any date if you have not.)
      `the last day of the period the Secretary of State specified` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period the Secretary of State specified for accepting a claimant commitment?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my claimant commitment treated as accepted where my award is made without a claim` IS
    `reg 15(2) — the day on which the claimant commitment is treated as accepted where an award may be made without a claim` `the day that would be the first day of my first assessment period` (IF `I have accepted a claimant commitment` THEN JUST `the day I accepted it` ELSE NOTHING) `the last day of the period the Secretary of State specified`

-- reg 15(4). You must accept a claimant commitment electronically, by telephone or in writing, as the Secretary of State specifies.
@export Must I accept my claimant commitment in the way the Secretary of State specifies, and did I (reg 15(4))?
GIVEN `the way I accepted it` IS A `Method of accepting a claimant commitment` @desc How did you accept your claimant commitment (electronically, by telephone, or in writing)?
      `the way the Secretary of State specified` IS A `Method of accepting a claimant commitment` @desc How did the Secretary of State specify that you must accept it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I accept my claimant commitment in the way the Secretary of State specified` IF
    `reg 15(4) — the claimant commitment was accepted by the method the Secretary of State specified` `the way I accepted it` `the way the Secretary of State specified`

-- reg 16. No need if the Secretary of State considers you lack the capacity to accept one, or that exceptional circumstances make it unreasonable to expect you to, or if you are terminally ill.
@export Do I not need to have accepted a claimant commitment (reg 16)?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers that I lack the capacity to accept a claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State decided that you cannot accept a claimant commitment because you lack the capacity to do so?
      `the Secretary of State considers that exceptional circumstances make it unreasonable to expect me to accept one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State decided that there are exceptional circumstances in which it would be unreasonable to expect you to accept one?
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `the months within which my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many months can your death in consequence of that disease reasonably be expected? (Any number if there is no progressive disease.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I not need to have accepted a claimant commitment` IF
    `reg 16 — the person does not have to meet the basic condition to have accepted a claimant commitment` `the Secretary of State considers that I lack the capacity to accept a claimant commitment` `the Secretary of State considers that exceptional circumstances make it unreasonable to expect me to accept one` `I am terminally ill`
    WHERE
        `my illness` MEANS Illness WITH
            `suffering from a progressive disease` IS `I suffer from a progressive disease`
            `months within which death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS `the months within which my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected`
        `I am terminally ill` MEANS
            `reg 2 — terminally ill` `my illness`

§§ `Money limits and who is barred (regulations 17 to 19)`

@export Is the amount payable to me at least the minimum, one penny (reg 17)?
GIVEN `the amount payable to me, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount payable to you for the assessment period, in pounds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the amount payable to me at least the minimum` IF
    `reg 17 — the amount payable is not less than the minimum` `the amount payable to me, in pounds`

@export What is the capital limit for my claim, in pounds (reg 18(1))?
GIVEN `how I claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc How are you claiming (as a single claimant, as joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the capital limit for my claim` IS
    `reg 18(1) — the prescribed capital amount` `how I claim`

-- reg 18. The limit is £16,000. A member of a couple who claims as a single person is treated as having the other member's capital too, and so, in this reading, are joint claimants (fork F-18-JOINT). What counts as capital is for the rules on income and capital (piece uc2), so the amounts are asked as given.
@export Is my capital within the limit (reg 18)?
GIVEN `how I claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc How are you claiming (as a single claimant, as joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple)?
      `my capital, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much capital do you have, in pounds?
      `my partner's capital, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much capital does your partner have, in pounds? (0 if you have no partner.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my capital within the limit` IF
    `reg 18(1) — the capital is within the limit` `how I claim` (`reg 18(2) — the capital taken into account` `how I claim` `my capital, in pounds` `my partner's capital, in pounds`)

-- reg 19(4). Detained under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983 before the release date the Secretary of State certifies (if any), or under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 or section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003.
@export Am I serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital (reg 19(4))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
      `a certified release date exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State certified a release date for you (within the meaning of section 50(3) of the Mental Health Act 1983)?
      `my certified release date` IS A DATE @desc What is the certified release date? (Any date if there is none.)
      `the person is being detained under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you being detained under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983 (a direction to hospital, or the removal to hospital of a person serving a sentence)?
      `the person is being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995 (hospital direction)?
      `the person is being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 (transfer of prisoners for treatment of mental disorder)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` IF
    `reg 19(4) — the person is serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` `my detention` `the day I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `my detention` MEANS `Person who may be serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` WITH
            `the person is being detained under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS `the person is being detained under section 45A or 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983`
            `release date that the Secretary of State certifies, within the meaning of section 50(3) of that Act` IS IF `a certified release date exists` THEN JUST `my certified release date` ELSE NOTHING
            `the person is being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995` IS `the person is being detained under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995`
            `the person is being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS `the person is being detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`

-- reg 19(2). A prisoner is not barred in the first 6 months if entitled as a single person immediately before becoming a prisoner with housing costs in the award, and not sentenced to a term in custody expected to extend beyond those 6 months.
@export Does the exception for the first 6 months as a prisoner apply to me (reg 19(2))?
GIVEN `the day I became a prisoner` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you become a prisoner?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
      `I was entitled to universal credit as a single person immediately before becoming a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to Universal Credit as a single person immediately before you became a prisoner?
      `my award then included an amount for the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the calculation of that award include an amount for the housing costs element?
      `my sentence is expected to extend beyond those 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond those 6 months?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the exception for the first 6 months as a prisoner apply to me` IF
    `reg 19(2) — paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` `the day I became a prisoner` `the day I am asking about` `I was entitled to universal credit as a single person immediately before becoming a prisoner` `my award then included an amount for the housing costs element` `my sentence is expected to extend beyond those 6 months`

-- reg 19(1). No entitlement arises for a member of a religious order fully maintained by it, a prisoner (except as paragraph (2) provides) or a person serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital. Two facts are the answers to the questions on regulation 19(2) and 19(4).
@export Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital (reg 19(1))?
GIVEN `I am a member of a religious order who is fully maintained by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a religious order who is fully maintained by your order?
      `I am detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction?
      `I am detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court?
      `I am on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you on temporary release in accordance with the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989?
      `I am detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in hospital under the Mental Health Act 1983 or, in Scotland, under the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 or the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995?
      `the exception in regulation 19(2) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on the first 6 months as a prisoner (regulation 19(2)) give the answer yes?
      `I am serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital (regulation 19(4)) give the answer yes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my entitlement barred because I am a prisoner, in a religious order or detained in hospital` IF
    `reg 19(1) — entitlement does not arise` `I am a member of a religious order who is fully maintained by it` `I am a prisoner` `the exception in regulation 19(2) applies to me` `I am serving a sentence of imprisonment detained in hospital`
    WHERE
        `my detention` MEANS Detention WITH
            `detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction` IS `I am detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction`
            `detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court` IS `I am detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court`
            `on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989` IS `I am on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989`
            `detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS `I am detained in hospital under the mental health Acts`
        `I am a prisoner` MEANS
            `reg 2 — prisoner` `my detention`

-- reg 19(3). In the case of a prisoner to whom paragraph (2) applies, an award includes no element other than the housing costs element.
@export May my award include a given element while I am a prisoner in my first 6 months (reg 19(3))?
GIVEN `the element I am asking about` IS AN `Element of an award` @desc Which element are you asking about (standard allowance, child element, housing costs element, LCWRA element, carer element, childcare costs element)?
      `I am a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies (see the previous question)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my award include a given element while I am a prisoner in my first 6 months` IF
    `reg 19(3) — the award may include the element` `the element I am asking about` `I am a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies`

§§ `When my months run and how my award is worked out (regulations 21 to 22A)`

-- reg 21(1), (2). An assessment period is a month beginning on the day of the first date of entitlement (the 29th, 30th or 31st are adjusted for short months). Number 0 is the first.
@export On what day does my assessment period number n begin (reg 21(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your first date of entitlement (the day your Universal Credit entitlement began)?
      `the number of months after my first date of entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months after your first date of entitlement does the period begin? (0 for the first period.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my assessment period number n begin` IS
    `reg 21(2) — the first day of an assessment period` `my first date of entitlement` `the number of months after my first date of entitlement`

-- reg 21(1). NOTHING if the day is before the first date of entitlement.
@export On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day begin (reg 21(1))?
GIVEN `my first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your first date of entitlement?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day begin` IS
    CONSIDER `reg 21(1) — the assessment period containing a day` `my first date of entitlement` `the day I am asking about`
    WHEN JUST period THEN JUST (period's `first day`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day end (reg 21(1))?
GIVEN `my first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your first date of entitlement?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the assessment period that includes a given day end` IS
    CONSIDER `reg 21(1) — the assessment period containing a day` `my first date of entitlement` `the day I am asking about`
    WHEN JUST period THEN JUST (period's `last day`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- reg 21(3). Answer: the first date of entitlement whose cycle the new award follows, or NOTHING.
@export Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I am a single person awarded Universal Credit without a claim (reg 21(3))?
GIVEN `my new award is made to me as a single person without a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your new award made to you as a single person without a claim, because your old award ended when you stopped being a member of a couple (regulation 9(6)(a) or (10) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 2013)?
      `the first date of entitlement of my old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the first date of entitlement of my old award?
      `the last day of the last assessment period of my old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the last assessment period of my old award?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I am a single person awarded Universal Credit without a claim` IS
    `reg 21(3) — the first date of entitlement whose cycle the new award follows` `my new award is made to me as a single person without a claim` `my old award`
    WHERE
        `my old award` MEANS `Old award whose assessment periods a new award follows` WITH
            `first date of entitlement of the old award` IS `the first date of entitlement of my old award`
            `last day of the old award's last assessment period` IS `the last day of the last assessment period of my old award`

-- reg 21(3A). The cycle of whichever old award ended earlier is followed.
@export Do our assessment periods follow an earlier award when we are a couple awarded Universal Credit jointly without a claim (reg 21(3A))?
GIVEN `our new award is made to us as a couple jointly without a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your new award made to you and your partner jointly without a claim, because two previous awards ended when you formed a couple (regulation 9(6)(b) or (7) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 2013)?
      `the first date of entitlement of my old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the first date of entitlement of my old award?
      `the last day of the last assessment period of my old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the last assessment period of my old award?
      `the first date of entitlement of my partner's old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the first date of entitlement of my partner's old award?
      `the last day of the last assessment period of my partner's old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the last assessment period of my partner's old award?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Do our assessment periods follow an earlier award when we are a couple awarded Universal Credit jointly without a claim` IS
    `reg 21(3A) — the first date of entitlement whose cycle the new award follows` `our new award is made to us as a couple jointly without a claim` `my old award` `my partner's old award`
    WHERE
        `my old award` MEANS `Old award whose assessment periods a new award follows` WITH
            `first date of entitlement of the old award` IS `the first date of entitlement of my old award`
            `last day of the old award's last assessment period` IS `the last day of the last assessment period of my old award`
        `my partner's old award` MEANS `Old award whose assessment periods a new award follows` WITH
            `first date of entitlement of the old award` IS `the first date of entitlement of my partner's old award`
            `last day of the old award's last assessment period` IS `the last day of the last assessment period of my partner's old award`

@export Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when my claim is treated as made under regulation 9(8) of the Claims and Payments Regulations (reg 21(3B))?
GIVEN `my claim is treated as made by virtue of regulation 9(8) of the Claims and Payments Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim treated as made by virtue of regulation 9(8) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 2013 (your old award ended when you formed a couple with a person not entitled to Universal Credit)?
      `the first date of entitlement of my old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the first date of entitlement of my old award?
      `the last day of the last assessment period of my old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the last assessment period of my old award?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when my claim is treated as made under regulation 9(8) of the Claims and Payments Regulations` IS
    `reg 21(3B) — the first date of entitlement whose cycle the new award follows` `my claim is treated as made by virtue of regulation 9(8) of the Claims and Payments Regulations` `my old award`
    WHERE
        `my old award` MEANS `Old award whose assessment periods a new award follows` WITH
            `first date of entitlement of the old award` IS `the first date of entitlement of my old award`
            `last day of the old award's last assessment period` IS `the last day of the last assessment period of my old award`

-- reg 21(3C). Where there was an old award for each of two joint claimants, the cycle of whichever ended earlier is followed.
@export Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I claim within 6 months of its end (reg 21(3C))?
GIVEN `the day I made the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the claim?
      `the last day of my previous award` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the previous award?
      `during those 6 months I continued to meet the basic conditions in section 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the 6 months before the claim, did you continue to meet the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act? Leave out the requirement to have accepted a claimant commitment, and any temporary absence from Great Britain that would be disregarded during entitlement.
      `during those 6 months regulation 19 did not exclude me from entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During those 6 months, were you not excluded from entitlement by regulation 19?
      `the first date of entitlement of my first old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the first date of entitlement of my first old award?
      `the last day of the last assessment period of my first old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the last assessment period of my first old award?
      `there was an old award for each of two joint claimants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there an old award for each of two joint claimants?
      `the first date of entitlement of the second old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the first date of entitlement of the second old award?
      `the last day of the last assessment period of the second old award` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the last assessment period of the second old award?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Do my assessment periods follow an earlier award when I claim within 6 months of its end` IS
    `reg 21(3C) — the first date of entitlement whose cycle the new award follows` `my claim` `my first old award` (IF `there was an old award for each of two joint claimants` THEN JUST `my second old award` ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        `my claim` MEANS `Claim made within 6 months of the end of a previous award` WITH
            `date on which the claim is made` IS `the day I made the claim`
            `last day of the previous award` IS `the last day of my previous award`
            `during those 6 months the claimant continued to meet the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act` IS `during those 6 months I continued to meet the basic conditions in section 4`
            `during those 6 months the claimant was not excluded from entitlement by regulation 19` IS `during those 6 months regulation 19 did not exclude me from entitlement`
        `my first old award` MEANS `Old award whose assessment periods a new award follows` WITH
            `first date of entitlement of the old award` IS `the first date of entitlement of my first old award`
            `last day of the old award's last assessment period` IS `the last day of the last assessment period of my first old award`
        `my second old award` MEANS `Old award whose assessment periods a new award follows` WITH
            `first date of entitlement of the old award` IS `the first date of entitlement of the second old award`
            `last day of the old award's last assessment period` IS `the last day of the last assessment period of the second old award`

-- reg 21(3D). The answer is yes (it does not matter) when the case is one to which paragraph (3B) or (3C) applies and the member meets the basic conditions in section 4(1)(a) and (c) and is not excluded by regulation 19 at the end of the first assessment period.
@export Does it not matter that I was below the minimum age, outside Great Britain or excluded by regulation 19 at the start of my first assessment period (reg 21(3D))?
GIVEN `paragraph (3B) or (3C) applies to my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph (3B) or (3C) of regulation 21 apply to your case?
      `I meet the basic conditions in section 4(1)(a) and (c) and am not excluded by regulation 19 at the end of the first assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of your first assessment period, did you meet the basic conditions in section 4(1)(a) and (c) of the Act and were you not excluded by regulation 19?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does it not matter that I was below the minimum age, outside Great Britain or excluded by regulation 19 at the start of my first assessment period` IF
    `reg 21(3D) — the member's position at the beginning of the first assessment period does not matter` `paragraph (3B) or (3C) applies to my case` `I meet the basic conditions in section 4(1)(a) and (c) and am not excluded by regulation 19 at the end of the first assessment period`

-- reg 21. If one of the paragraphs (3), (3A), (3B) or (3C) gives an earlier award's cycle to follow, my periods run from that date; otherwise from my own first date of entitlement. The four answers are those of the four questions above.
@export From which date do my assessment periods run (reg 21)?
GIVEN `my own first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your own first date of entitlement?
      `paragraph (3) gives me a cycle to follow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 21(3) give a date (rather than NOTHING)?
      `the date given under paragraph (3)` IS A DATE @desc What date did it give? (Any date if it gave none.)
      `paragraph (3A) gives me a cycle to follow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 21(3A) give a date (rather than NOTHING)?
      `the date given under paragraph (3A)` IS A DATE @desc What date did it give? (Any date if it gave none.)
      `paragraph (3B) gives me a cycle to follow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 21(3B) give a date (rather than NOTHING)?
      `the date given under paragraph (3B)` IS A DATE @desc What date did it give? (Any date if it gave none.)
      `paragraph (3C) gives me a cycle to follow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 21(3C) give a date (rather than NOTHING)?
      `the date given under paragraph (3C)` IS A DATE @desc What date did it give? (Any date if it gave none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which date do my assessment periods run` IS
    `reg 21 — the first date of entitlement from which the assessment periods run` `my own first date of entitlement` (IF `paragraph (3) gives me a cycle to follow` THEN JUST `the date given under paragraph (3)` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `paragraph (3A) gives me a cycle to follow` THEN JUST `the date given under paragraph (3A)` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `paragraph (3B) gives me a cycle to follow` THEN JUST `the date given under paragraph (3B)` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `paragraph (3C) gives me a cycle to follow` THEN JUST `the date given under paragraph (3C)` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Does regulation 21A keep my assessment period cycle the same after a change in my first date of entitlement (reg 21A(1))?
GIVEN `the first date of entitlement has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your first date of entitlement been determined?
      `it is subsequently determined that the first date of entitlement falls on a different date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it subsequently been determined that your first date of entitlement falls on a different date?
      `in the opinion of the Secretary of State applying regulation 21(1) and (2) would cause unnecessary disruption to the administration of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion, would applying regulation 21(1) and (2) cause unnecessary disruption to the administration of your claim?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 21A keep my assessment period cycle the same after a change in my first date of entitlement` IF
    `reg 21A(1) — this regulation applies` `my change`
    WHERE
        `my change` MEANS `Change in the first date of entitlement` WITH
            `the first date of entitlement has been determined` IS `the first date of entitlement has been determined`
            `it is subsequently determined that the first date of entitlement falls on a different date` IS `it is subsequently determined that the first date of entitlement falls on a different date`
            `in the opinion of the Secretary of State applying regulation 21(1) and (2) would cause unnecessary disruption to the administration of the claim` IS `in the opinion of the Secretary of State applying regulation 21(1) and (2) would cause unnecessary disruption to the administration of the claim`

@export What are the first and last days of my first assessment period after the change (reg 21A(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my start date` IS A DATE @desc What is the start date (the day the first assessment period begins)?
      `the last day of the first assessment period as the Secretary of State determines` IS A DATE @desc What last day of the first assessment period has the Secretary of State determined?
GIVETH A `Assessment period`
DECIDE `What are the first and last days of my first assessment period after the change` IS
    `reg 21A(2)(a) — the first assessment period` `my start date` `the last day of the first assessment period as the Secretary of State determines`

-- reg 21A(2)(b). The text in the source ends the sentence at the variable definitions and does not show the formula (fork F-FORMULA), so the answer is always NOTHING.
@export What amount is payable for my first assessment period after the change (reg 21A(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the first day of that period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of that first assessment period?
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that first assessment period?
      `the amount calculated as if the period were an assessment period of a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount would be payable if the period were an ordinary assessment period of one month, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What amount is payable for my first assessment period after the change` IS
    `reg 21A(2)(b) — the amount payable for the first assessment period` `that period` `the amount calculated as if the period were an assessment period of a month`
    WHERE
        `that period` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `the first day of that period`
            `last day` IS `the last day of that period`

@export From which date do my later assessment periods run after the change (reg 21A(2)(c))?
GIVEN `the first day of that period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the first assessment period?
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the first assessment period?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which date do my later assessment periods run after the change` IS
    `reg 21A(2)(c) — the first date of entitlement from which the second and later assessment periods run` `that period`
    WHERE
        `that period` MEANS `Assessment period` WITH
            `first day` IS `the first day of that period`
            `last day` IS `the last day of that period`

-- reg 22(2). NOTHING means no work allowance applies to me.
@export What is my work allowance (reg 22(2))?
GIVEN `my award contains an amount for the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your award contain an amount for the housing costs element?
      `I am responsible for a child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or, if you claim jointly, either of you) responsible for a child or qualifying young person?
      `I have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you (or, if you claim jointly, one or both of you) have limited capability for work?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my work allowance` IS
    `reg 22(2) — the work allowance` `my award contains an amount for the housing costs element` `I am responsible for a child or qualifying young person` `I have limited capability for work`

@export What income of mine and my partner's is taken into account (reg 22(3))?
GIVEN `how I claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc How are you claiming (as a single claimant, as joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple)?
      `my income for the assessment period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your income for the assessment period, in pounds?
      `my partner's income for the assessment period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your partner's income for the assessment period, in pounds? (0 if you have no partner.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What income of mine and my partner's is taken into account` IS
    `reg 22(3) — the income taken into account` `how I claim` `my income for the assessment period, in pounds` `my partner's income for the assessment period, in pounds`

-- reg 22(1). All of the unearned income, plus 55% of the earned income (or, where there is a work allowance, 55% of the amount by which the earned income exceeds it).
@export How much is deducted from my maximum amount for my income (reg 22(1))?
GIVEN `my unearned income taken into account, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What unearned income is taken into account for the assessment period, in pounds?
      `my earned income taken into account, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What earned income is taken into account for the assessment period, in pounds?
      `my award contains an amount for the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your award contain an amount for the housing costs element?
      `I am responsible for a child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or, if you claim jointly, either of you) responsible for a child or qualifying young person?
      `I have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you (or, if you claim jointly, one or both of you) have limited capability for work?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is deducted from my maximum amount for my income` IS
    `reg 22(1) — the amount deducted from the maximum amount` `my unearned income taken into account, in pounds` `my earned income taken into account, in pounds` (`reg 22(2) — the work allowance` `my award contains an amount for the housing costs element` `I am responsible for a child or qualifying young person` `I have limited capability for work`)

-- reg 22(1). The maximum amount of the award (regulation 23) less the amount deducted for income (section 8(3) of the Act). The difference is not floored at nothing (see NOTES.md, finding on regulation 22).
@export How much Universal Credit am I awarded for an assessment period (reg 22(1))?
GIVEN `my maximum amount, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum amount of your award for the assessment period, in pounds (see the question on regulation 23)?
      `the amount deducted for my income, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is deducted for your income, in pounds (see the previous question)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much Universal Credit am I awarded for an assessment period` IS
    `reg 22(1) — the amount of an award` `my maximum amount, in pounds` `the amount deducted for my income, in pounds`

@export Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job (reg 22A(1))?
GIVEN `my new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your new award made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies (see the question on it)?
      `I am not in paid work (nor is either joint claimant)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or, if you claim jointly, is either of you) not in paid work?
      `the day I ceased paid work` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease paid work?
      `the last day of my previous award` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of your previous award?
      `the day I made the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the claim?
      `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for my delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that there is good reason for the delay in making your claim?
      `the number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Secretary of State has extended the period, how many days is the extended period? (0 if not extended.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 22A apply because I re-claimed late after losing my job` IF
    `reg 22A(1) — this regulation applies` `my reclaim`
    WHERE
        `my reclaim` MEANS `Reclaim after loss of employment` WITH
            `the new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies` IS `my new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies`
            `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is not in paid work` IS `I am not in paid work (nor is either joint claimant)`
            `day on which the claimant ceased paid work` IS `the day I ceased paid work`
            `last day of the previous award` IS `the last day of my previous award`
            `date on which the claim is made` IS `the day I made the claim`
            `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for the delay in making the claim` IS `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for my delay`
            `number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it` IS `the number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it`

@export How many days end with the day of my claim, for regulation 22A (reg 22A(3))?
GIVEN `my new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your new award made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies (see the question on it)?
      `I am not in paid work (nor is either joint claimant)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or, if you claim jointly, is either of you) not in paid work?
      `the day I ceased paid work` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease paid work?
      `the last day of my previous award` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of your previous award?
      `the day I made the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the claim?
      `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for my delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that there is good reason for the delay in making your claim?
      `the number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Secretary of State has extended the period, how many days is the extended period? (0 if not extended.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days end with the day of my claim, for regulation 22A` IS
    `reg 22A(3) — the number of days ending with the day of the claim` `my reclaim`
    WHERE
        `my reclaim` MEANS `Reclaim after loss of employment` WITH
            `the new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies` IS `my new award is made in a case to which regulation 21(3C) applies`
            `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is not in paid work` IS `I am not in paid work (nor is either joint claimant)`
            `day on which the claimant ceased paid work` IS `the day I ceased paid work`
            `last day of the previous award` IS `the last day of my previous award`
            `date on which the claim is made` IS `the day I made the claim`
            `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for the delay in making the claim` IS `the Secretary of State considers there is good reason for my delay`
            `number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it` IS `the number of days in the period as the Secretary of State extends it`

@export How many days run from my claim to the end of the assessment period (reg 22A(2))?
GIVEN `the day I made the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the claim?
      `the last day of the assessment period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the assessment period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days run from my claim to the end of the assessment period` IS
    `reg 22A(2) — the number of days from the claim to the end of the assessment period` `the day I made the claim` `the last day of the assessment period`

-- reg 22A(2). The source text does not show the formula for the reduction (fork F-FORMULA), so the answer is always NOTHING.
@export What is the reduced amount for the days after my late re-claim (reg 22A(2))?
GIVEN `the amount that would otherwise be payable or deducted, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount would otherwise be payable or deducted for the assessment period, in pounds?
      `the number of days from my claim to the end of the assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days run from your claim to the end of the assessment period (see the previous question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the reduced amount for the days after my late re-claim` IS
    `reg 22A(2) — the reduced amount` `the amount that would otherwise be payable or deducted, in pounds` `the number of days from my claim to the end of the assessment period`

§§ `What my award is made of: elements, children and housing costs (regulations 23 to 26)`

-- reg 23(1). The sum of the amounts of the elements that apply: standard allowance, child element, housing costs element, LCWRA element, carer element and childcare costs element. Enter 0 for an element you do not get.
@export What is the maximum amount of my award, in pounds (reg 23(1))?
GIVEN `my standard allowance, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your standard allowance for the assessment period, in pounds (see the question on regulation 36)?
      `my child element, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your child element, in pounds (see the question on regulation 24)?
      `my housing costs element, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your housing costs element, in pounds (see the question on regulation 26)?
      `my LCWRA element, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your limited capability for work and work-related activity element, in pounds (see the question on regulation 27)?
      `my carer element, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your carer element, in pounds (see the question on regulation 29)?
      `my childcare costs element, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your childcare costs element, in pounds (see the question on regulation 34)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the maximum amount of my award` IS
    `reg 23(1) — the maximum amount of an award` `my elements`
    WHERE
        `my elements` MEANS `Amounts of the elements of an award` WITH
            `the standard allowance` IS `my standard allowance, in pounds`
            `the child element` IS `my child element, in pounds`
            `the housing costs element` IS `my housing costs element, in pounds`
            `the LCWRA element` IS `my LCWRA element, in pounds`
            `the carer element` IS `my carer element, in pounds`
            `the childcare costs element` IS `my childcare costs element, in pounds`

@export Is an element one that section 12 of the Act includes in an award (reg 23(2))?
GIVEN `the element I am asking about` IS AN `Element of an award` @desc Which element are you asking about (standard allowance, child element, housing costs element, LCWRA element, carer element, childcare costs element)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an element one that section 12 of the Act includes in an award` IF
    `reg 23(2) — an element included under section 12 of the Act` `the element I am asking about`

-- reg 24(2). The higher rate if the child or young person is entitled to the highest-rate care component or enhanced-rate daily living component of a listed benefit, or is blind; the lower rate if entitled to one of the listed benefits; otherwise no additional amount.
@export What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person (reg 24(2))?
GIVEN `the child or young person is entitled to a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or qualifying young person entitled to disability living allowance, Scottish adult disability living allowance, child disability payment, adult disability payment or personal independence payment?
      `the benefit the child or young person is entitled to` IS A Benefit @desc Which of those benefits is the child or qualifying young person entitled to? (If more than one, choose any one.)
      `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or young person entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate?
      `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate?
      `entitled to the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they entitled to the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate?
      `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate?
      `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate?
      `the child or young person is certified as severely sight impaired or blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they certified as severely sight impaired or blind?
      `the child or young person's certificate was given by a consultant ophthalmologist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that certificate given by a consultant ophthalmologist?
GIVETH A `Rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person`
DECIDE `What rate of additional amount do I get for a disabled child or young person` IS
    `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `the child or young person`
    WHERE
        `the child or young person` MEANS `Entitlements of a child or qualifying young person to the additional amount` WITH
            `entitled to` IS IF `the child or young person is entitled to a benefit` THEN LIST `the benefit the child or young person is entitled to` ELSE EMPTY
            `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate`
            `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate`
            `entitled to the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate` IS `entitled to the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate`
            `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate` IS `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate`
            `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate` IS `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate`
            `sight certificate` IS `the sight certificate`
        `the sight certificate` MEANS `Sight certificate` WITH
            `certified as severely sight impaired or blind` IS `the child or young person is certified as severely sight impaired or blind`
            `certified by a consultant ophthalmologist` IS `the child or young person's certificate was given by a consultant ophthalmologist`

@export How much is the child element of my award, in pounds (reg 24)?
GIVEN `the number of children and qualifying young persons I am responsible for` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many children and qualifying young persons are you responsible?
      `the number of them who are disabled and get the lower rate` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are disabled and get the lower rate of additional amount?
      `the number of them who are disabled and get the higher rate` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are disabled and get the higher rate of additional amount?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the child element of my award` IS
    `reg 24 — the amount of the child elements` `the number of children and qualifying young persons I am responsible for` `the number of them who are disabled and get the lower rate` `the number of them who are disabled and get the higher rate`

-- reg 25. The element is included if you are liable to make payments in respect of accommodation (rent payments or service charge payments), the liability is on a commercial basis or treated as liability under Schedule 2, and you occupy the accommodation as your home or are treated as doing so under Schedule 3. The Schedules are not inputs: you are asked for their results.
@export Do I meet the conditions for the housing costs element (reg 25)?
GIVEN `the payments are rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1?
      `the payments are service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1?
      `the claimant, or either joint claimant, has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you (or either of you, if you claim jointly) have a liability to make the payments that is on a commercial basis?
      `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or either of you) treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments?
      `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treats the claimant, or either joint claimant, as not being liable to make the payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treat you (or either of you) as not being liable to make the payments?
      `the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as your home?
      `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 3 treats the claimant as not occupying that accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 3 treat you as not occupying that accommodation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the conditions for the housing costs element` IF
    `reg 25(5)(b) — the claimant meets all of the conditions specified in this regulation` `my payments` `my liability` `my occupation`
    WHERE
        `my payments` MEANS `Payments in respect of accommodation` WITH
            `the payments are rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1` IS `the payments are rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1`
            `the payments are service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1` IS `the payments are service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1`
        `my liability` MEANS `Liability of a claimant to make payments in respect of accommodation` WITH
            `the claimant, or either joint claimant, has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis` IS `the claimant, or either joint claimant, has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis`
            `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments` IS `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments`
            `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treats the claimant, or either joint claimant, as not being liable to make the payments` IS `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treats the claimant, or either joint claimant, as not being liable to make the payments`
        `my occupation` MEANS `Occupation of accommodation by a claimant` WITH
            `the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home` IS `the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home`
            `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 3 treats the claimant as not occupying that accommodation` IS `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 3 treats the claimant as not occupying that accommodation`

@export Is my tenancy a shared ownership tenancy (reg 26(6))?
GIVEN `nation in which the accommodation is` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the accommodation?
      `a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of the accommodation or the cost of providing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of the accommodation or the cost of providing it?
      `an agreement under which the tenant, who with the landlord jointly owns the accommodation, is the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an agreement under which you, who with the landlord jointly own the accommodation, are the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest?
      `an agreement under which the tenant has the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an agreement under which you have the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest in it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my tenancy a shared ownership tenancy` IF
    `reg 26(6) — a shared ownership tenancy` `my tenancy`
    WHERE
        `my tenancy` MEANS `Tenancy that may be a shared ownership tenancy` WITH
            `nation in which the accommodation is` IS `nation in which the accommodation is`
            `a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of the accommodation or the cost of providing it` IS `a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of the accommodation or the cost of providing it`
            `an agreement under which the tenant, who with the landlord jointly owns the accommodation, is the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest` IS `an agreement under which the tenant, who with the landlord jointly owns the accommodation, is the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest`
            `an agreement under which the tenant has the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest in it` IS `an agreement under which the tenant has the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest in it`

-- reg 26(2) to (4). Schedule 4 applies where the payments are rent payments (whether or not service charge payments are also payable), Schedule 5 where they are service charge payments, and for a shared ownership tenancy to which both apply an amount is calculated under each and the two are added. The text does not say what happens to a tenant who is not in shared ownership and to whom both apply (fork F-26-OVERLAP), and the answer says so.
@export Which Schedule decides the amount of my housing costs element (reg 26(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `I meet all the conditions in regulation 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet all the conditions in regulation 25 (see the previous question)?
      `my payments are rent payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for which you are liable rent payments?
      `my payments are service charge payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for which you are liable service charge payments?
      `I occupy the accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you occupy the accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy (see the question on regulation 26(6))?
GIVETH A `Schedules that have effect for the amount of the housing costs element`
DECIDE `Which Schedule decides the amount of my housing costs element` IS
    `reg 26(2) to (4) — the Schedules that have effect` `I meet all the conditions in regulation 25` `my payments are rent payments` `my payments are service charge payments` `I occupy the accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy`

-- reg 26(4). NOTHING means the case is not covered by the regulation.
@export How much is my housing costs element, in pounds (reg 26(4))?
GIVEN `the Schedules that decide my housing costs element` IS A `Schedules that have effect for the amount of the housing costs element` @desc Which Schedule decides the amount (see the previous question)?
      `the amount under Schedule 4, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does Schedule 4 give you, in pounds? (0 if it does not apply.)
      `the amount under Schedule 5, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does Schedule 5 give you, in pounds? (0 if it does not apply.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my housing costs element` IS
    `reg 26(4) — the amount of the housing costs element` `the Schedules that decide my housing costs element` `the amount under Schedule 4, in pounds` `the amount under Schedule 5, in pounds`

-- reg 26(5). Yes only in a case to which paragraph (4) applies (both Schedules, for a shared ownership tenancy) where there is a liability for service charge payments; for any other case this paragraph says nothing, and the answer is no.
@export Is the amount for my service charge payments worked out under Schedule 4 because of my shared ownership tenancy (reg 26(5))?
GIVEN `the Schedules that decide my housing costs element` IS A `Schedules that have effect for the amount of the housing costs element` @desc Which Schedule decides the amount (see the question on regulation 26(2) to (4))?
      `I am liable for service charge payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable for service charge payments?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the amount for my service charge payments worked out under Schedule 4 because of my shared ownership tenancy` IF
    `reg 26(5) — the amount for the service charge payments is calculated under Schedule 4` `the Schedules that decide my housing costs element` `I am liable for service charge payments`

§§ `Extra for illness, disability and caring (regulations 27 to 30)`

-- reg 27A(1). A claimant entitled to an award that included the LCWRA element before 6 April 2026 and continuously since (periods of non-entitlement that regulation 27A(2) disregards do not count), or a claimant who meets a circumstance in Schedule 5A.
@export Am I a pre-2026 claimant for the LCWRA element (reg 27A(1))?
GIVEN `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `I was entitled to an award that included the LCWRA element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ever been entitled to an award of Universal Credit that included the LCWRA element?
      `the earliest day on which I was entitled to such an award` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you first entitled to such an award? (Any date if never.)
      `I have had a period of non-entitlement since that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since that day, have you had a period when you were not entitled to Universal Credit?
      `that period began because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or (2)(b) ceased to be met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that period begin because the amount payable to you fell below the minimum (the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or (2)(b) of the Act)?
      `the day the condition ceased to be met` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that condition cease to be met? (Any date if there was no such period.)
      `the last day of the period of non-entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of that period of non-entitlement? (Any date if there was none.)
      `I meet a circumstance in Schedule 5A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet a circumstance in Schedule 5A?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a pre-2026 claimant for the LCWRA element` IF
    `reg 27A(1) — the claimant is a pre-2026 claimant` `my entitlement history`
    WHERE
        `my entitlement history` MEANS `Claimant's entitlement to awards that included the LCWRA element` WITH
            `the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity`
            `earliest day on which the claimant was entitled to an award that included the LCWRA element` IS IF `I was entitled to an award that included the LCWRA element` THEN JUST `the earliest day on which I was entitled to such an award` ELSE NOTHING
            `periods of non-entitlement since that day` IS IF `I have had a period of non-entitlement since that day` THEN LIST `my period of non-entitlement` ELSE EMPTY
            `the claimant meets a circumstance in Schedule 5A` IS `I meet a circumstance in Schedule 5A`
        `my period of non-entitlement` MEANS `Period of non-entitlement to universal credit` WITH
            `the period began because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or (2)(b) of the Act ceased to be met` IS `that period began because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or (2)(b) ceased to be met`
            `day on which that condition ceased to be met` IS `the day the condition ceased to be met`
            `last day of the period of non-entitlement` IS `the last day of the period of non-entitlement`

-- reg 27(1), (2). NOTHING if you do not have limited capability for work and work-related activity. The pre-2026 fact is the answer to the previous question.
@export How much LCWRA element do I get as a claimant, in pounds (reg 27(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work?
      `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `I am a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been determined, on an assessment under Part 5 (regulation 40A), that you are a severe conditions criteria claimant?
      `I am a pre-2026 claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 27A(1) give the answer yes?
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `the months within which my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many months can your death in consequence of that disease reasonably be expected? (Any number if there is no progressive disease.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much LCWRA element do I get as a claimant` IS
    `reg 27(1) and (2) — the amount of the LCWRA element for a claimant` `my capability for work` `I am a pre-2026 claimant` `I am terminally ill`
    WHERE
        `my capability for work` MEANS `Capability for work` WITH
            `limited capability for work` IS `I have limited capability for work`
            `limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity`
            `severe conditions criteria claimant` IS `I am a severe conditions criteria claimant`
        `my illness` MEANS Illness WITH
            `suffering from a progressive disease` IS `I suffer from a progressive disease`
            `months within which death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS `the months within which my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected`
        `I am terminally ill` MEANS
            `reg 2 — terminally ill` `my illness`

-- reg 27(4). The element for the joint claimants is that of whichever of them has the element, or the higher where both do; NOTHING if neither.
@export How much LCWRA element do we get as joint claimants, in pounds (reg 27(4))?
GIVEN `my LCWRA element is included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an LCWRA element included for you (see the previous question)?
      `my LCWRA element, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your LCWRA element, in pounds? (0 if none.)
      `my partner's LCWRA element is included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an LCWRA element included for your partner?
      `my partner's LCWRA element, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your partner's LCWRA element, in pounds? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much LCWRA element do we get as joint claimants` IS
    `reg 27(4) — the LCWRA element of joint claimants` (IF `my LCWRA element is included` THEN JUST `my LCWRA element, in pounds` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `my partner's LCWRA element is included` THEN JUST `my partner's LCWRA element, in pounds` ELSE NOTHING)

-- reg 28(1). The wait does not apply where, in the circumstances of paragraph (4), a previous award included the LCWRA element, or you are terminally ill, entitled to an ESA support component, or in the other cases of paragraphs (5) and (6).
@export Does the three-month wait for the LCWRA element apply to me (reg 28(1), (3) to (6))?
GIVEN `there was a previous award in the circumstances of regulation 28(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a previous award of Universal Credit that ended in the circumstances of regulation 28(4) (see the next two facts)?
      `immediately before the award commences the previous award ceased because the claimant ceased to be a member of a couple or became a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before this award began, did the previous award end because you stopped being, or became, a member of a couple?
      `within the six months before the award commences the previous award ceased because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or 5(2)(b) of the Act was not met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Within the six months before this award began, did the previous award end because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or (2)(b) of the Act was not met?
      `the previous award included the LCWRA element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the previous award include the LCWRA element?
      `the relevant period in relation to the previous award has begun but not ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the relevant period (the three months) in the previous award begun but not ended?
      `the day on which that relevant period would have ended in relation to the previous award` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day would that relevant period have ended in the previous award? (Any date if not.)
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `the months within which my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many months can your death in consequence of that disease reasonably be expected? (Any number if there is no progressive disease.)
      `the claimant is entitled to an employment and support allowance that includes the support component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an employment and support allowance that includes the support component?
      `the claimant was so entitled on the day before the award commenced and ceased to be so entitled by virtue of section 1A of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you so entitled on the day before this award began and did you cease to be so entitled by virtue of section 1A of the Welfare Reform Act 2007?
      `the claimant has limited capability for work and it is subsequently determined that they have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work, and has it since been determined that you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the three-month wait for the LCWRA element apply to me` IF
    `reg 28(1) — paragraph (1) applies` (IF `there was a previous award in the circumstances of regulation 28(4)` THEN JUST `my previous award` ELSE NOTHING) `my case`
    WHERE
        `my previous award` MEANS `Previous award of universal credit` WITH
            `immediately before the award commences the previous award ceased because the claimant ceased to be a member of a couple or became a member of a couple` IS `immediately before the award commences the previous award ceased because the claimant ceased to be a member of a couple or became a member of a couple`
            `within the six months before the award commences the previous award ceased because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or 5(2)(b) of the Act was not met` IS `within the six months before the award commences the previous award ceased because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or 5(2)(b) of the Act was not met`
            `the previous award included the LCWRA element` IS `the previous award included the LCWRA element`
            `the relevant period in relation to the previous award has begun but not ended` IS `the relevant period in relation to the previous award has begun but not ended`
            `the day on which that relevant period would have ended in relation to the previous award` IS `the day on which that relevant period would have ended in relation to the previous award`
        `my illness` MEANS Illness WITH
            `suffering from a progressive disease` IS `I suffer from a progressive disease`
            `months within which death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS `the months within which my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected`
        `I am terminally ill` MEANS
            `reg 2 — terminally ill` `my illness`
        `my case` MEANS `Claimant who may not be held back from the LCWRA element` WITH
            `the claimant is terminally ill` IS `I am terminally ill`
            `the claimant is entitled to an employment and support allowance that includes the support component` IS `the claimant is entitled to an employment and support allowance that includes the support component`
            `the claimant was so entitled on the day before the award commenced and ceased to be so entitled by virtue of section 1A of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` IS `the claimant was so entitled on the day before the award commenced and ceased to be so entitled by virtue of section 1A of the Welfare Reform Act 2007`
            `the claimant has limited capability for work and it is subsequently determined that they have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `the claimant has limited capability for work and it is subsequently determined that they have limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- reg 28(2), (3)(b). Three months from the first day of the relevant period, or the day it would have ended in a previous award.
@export On what day does the three-month wait for the LCWRA element end for me (reg 28(2), (3)(b))?
GIVEN `there was a previous award in the circumstances of regulation 28(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a previous award of Universal Credit that ended in the circumstances of regulation 28(4)?
      `I have applied for the LCWRA element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the LCWRA element to be included in your award?
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you apply? (Any date if you have not.)
      `regulation 41(2) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 41(2) apply to you (a claimant whose monthly earnings equal or exceed the relevant threshold)?
      `the day my award commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your award of Universal Credit commence?
      `the first day I provided evidence of limited capability for work` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first provide evidence of having limited capability for work under the Medical Evidence Regulations?
      `immediately before the award commences the previous award ceased because the claimant ceased to be a member of a couple or became a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before this award began, did the previous award end because you stopped being, or became, a member of a couple?
      `within the six months before the award commences the previous award ceased because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or 5(2)(b) of the Act was not met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Within the six months before this award began, did the previous award end because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or (2)(b) of the Act was not met?
      `the previous award included the LCWRA element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the previous award include the LCWRA element?
      `the relevant period in relation to the previous award has begun but not ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the relevant period (the three months) in the previous award begun but not ended?
      `the day on which that relevant period would have ended in relation to the previous award` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day would that relevant period have ended in the previous award? (Any date if not.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the three-month wait for the LCWRA element end for me` IS
    `reg 28(3)(b) — the last day of the relevant period, allowing for a previous award` `my start` (IF `there was a previous award in the circumstances of regulation 28(4)` THEN JUST `my previous award` ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        `my start` MEANS `Start of the relevant period for the LCWRA element` WITH
            `regulation 41(2) applies to the claimant` IS `regulation 41(2) applies to me`
            `day on which the award of universal credit commences` IS `the day my award commenced`
            `day on which the claimant applies for the LCWRA element to be included in the award` IS IF `I have applied for the LCWRA element` THEN JUST `the day I applied` ELSE NOTHING
            `first day on which the claimant provides evidence of having limited capability for work in accordance with the Medical Evidence Regulations` IS `the first day I provided evidence of limited capability for work`
        `my previous award` MEANS `Previous award of universal credit` WITH
            `immediately before the award commences the previous award ceased because the claimant ceased to be a member of a couple or became a member of a couple` IS `immediately before the award commences the previous award ceased because the claimant ceased to be a member of a couple or became a member of a couple`
            `within the six months before the award commences the previous award ceased because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or 5(2)(b) of the Act was not met` IS `within the six months before the award commences the previous award ceased because the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or 5(2)(b) of the Act was not met`
            `the previous award included the LCWRA element` IS `the previous award included the LCWRA element`
            `the relevant period in relation to the previous award has begun but not ended` IS `the relevant period in relation to the previous award has begun but not ended`
            `the day on which that relevant period would have ended in relation to the previous award` IS `the day on which that relevant period would have ended in relation to the previous award`

-- reg 28(1). The element starts with the assessment period after the one in which the wait ends; NOTHING if no assessment period contains that day.
@export From which day may my award include the LCWRA element, once the wait applies (reg 28(1))?
GIVEN `my first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your first date of entitlement?
      `the last day of my wait` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the wait end (see the previous question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which day may my award include the LCWRA element, once the wait applies` IS
    `reg 28(1) — the first day from which the award may include the LCWRA element` `my first date of entitlement` `the last day of my wait`

-- reg 28(7). One penny, where only the wait for the LCWRA element means the financial condition of section 5(1)(b) or (2)(b) is not met; otherwise NOTHING.
@export What is the amount payable to me during the wait if my income would otherwise stop my payment (reg 28(7))?
GIVEN `the financial condition is not met only because of the wait` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the financial condition in section 5(1)(b) or (2)(b) of the Act (the amount payable is not less than the minimum) unmet only because of the wait for the LCWRA element?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the amount payable to me during the wait if my income would otherwise stop my payment` IS
    `reg 28(7) — the amount payable during the relevant period` `the financial condition is not met only because of the wait`

-- reg 30. Whether or not you have claimed a carer's allowance (paragraph (2)); not if you earn income from the caring (paragraph (3)).
@export Do I have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person (reg 30)?
GIVEN `the person satisfies the conditions for entitlement to a carer's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions for entitlement to a carer's allowance?
      `the person would satisfy those conditions but for the fact that their earnings have exceeded the limit prescribed for that allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you satisfy them but for the fact that your earnings have exceeded the limit for that allowance?
      `the person would satisfy those conditions but for the fact that they are resident, or treated as resident, in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you satisfy them but for the fact that you are resident, or treated as resident, in Scotland?
      `the person would satisfy those conditions but for the fact that they are resident outside of Great Britain and have a genuine and sufficient link to Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you satisfy them but for the fact that you are resident outside Great Britain and have a genuine and sufficient link to Scotland?
      `the person is entitled to carer support payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to carer support payment?
      `the person derives earned income from those caring responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you derive earned income from those caring responsibilities?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` IF
    `reg 30 — regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` `my caring`
    WHERE
        `my caring` MEANS `Caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` WITH
            `the person satisfies the conditions for entitlement to a carer's allowance` IS `the person satisfies the conditions for entitlement to a carer's allowance`
            `the person would satisfy those conditions but for the fact that their earnings have exceeded the limit prescribed for that allowance` IS `the person would satisfy those conditions but for the fact that their earnings have exceeded the limit prescribed for that allowance`
            `the person would satisfy those conditions but for the fact that they are resident, or treated as resident, in Scotland` IS `the person would satisfy those conditions but for the fact that they are resident, or treated as resident, in Scotland`
            `the person would satisfy those conditions but for the fact that they are resident outside of Great Britain and have a genuine and sufficient link to Scotland` IS `the person would satisfy those conditions but for the fact that they are resident outside of Great Britain and have a genuine and sufficient link to Scotland`
            `the person is entitled to carer support payment` IS `the person is entitled to carer support payment`
            `the person derives earned income from those caring responsibilities` IS `the person derives earned income from those caring responsibilities`

-- reg 29(1) to (3). Where more than one person cares for the same severely disabled person, only one of them gets the element, by their joint election or the Secretary of State's decision.
@export May the carer element be included in my award (reg 29(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `I have regular and substantial caring responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person (see the previous question)?
      `section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act excludes me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 70 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 exclude you from the carer element?
      `two or more people care for the same severely disabled person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do two or more people have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for the same severely disabled person?
      `we have jointly elected me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they jointly elected you to have the element?
      `they made no election and the Secretary of State has chosen me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If they made no election, has the Secretary of State determined that you have it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the carer element be included in my award` IF
    `reg 29(1) to (3) — the carer element may be included for the claimant` `my caring`
    WHERE
        `my caring` MEANS `Claimant who may have the carer element` WITH
            `the claimant has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` IS `I have regular and substantial caring responsibilities`
            `section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act excludes the claimant from the carer element` IS `section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act excludes me`
            `two or more persons have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for the same severely disabled person` IS `two or more people care for the same severely disabled person`
            `those persons have jointly elected the claimant` IS `we have jointly elected me`
            `those persons have made no election and the Secretary of State determines the claimant` IS `they made no election and the Secretary of State has chosen me`

-- reg 29(4). A claimant who would get the carer element but also has limited capability for work and work-related activity gets only the LCWRA element (for joint claimants, so long as the LCWRA element has not been included for the other claimant).
@export Is only the LCWRA element included, so that I do not get the carer element too (reg 29(4))?
GIVEN `the carer element would be included for me by paragraphs (1) to (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the carer element be included for you (see the previous question)?
      `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `I am one of joint claimants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of joint claimants?
      `the LCWRA element has been included for my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the LCWRA element been included for your partner?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is only the LCWRA element included, so that I do not get the carer element too` IF
    `reg 29(4) — only the LCWRA element may be included` `the carer element would be included for me by paragraphs (1) to (3)` `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` `I am one of joint claimants` `the LCWRA element has been included for my partner`

@export May my award include the carer element when a Scottish entitlement is in question (reg 29(5), (6))?
GIVEN `person A has, or would have but for regulation 5(3) of the Carer's Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023, an entitlement to carer support payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Person A (the other carer) has, or would have but for regulation 5(3) of the Carer's Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023, an entitlement to carer support payment.
      `person A has, or would have but for section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act, an entitlement to carer's allowance in respect of which the Scottish Ministers have the power to make decisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Person A has, or would have but for section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act, an entitlement to carer's allowance on which the Scottish Ministers have the power to make decisions.
      `person B has, or would have but for regulation 29, an entitlement to the carer element for the same day in respect of the same severely disabled person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc You (person B) have, or would have but for regulation 29, an entitlement to the carer element for the same day for the same severely disabled person.
      `section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act does not apply to the decision in respect of B's entitlement to universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act does not apply to the decision on your entitlement to Universal Credit.
      `A and B jointly elect that B shall have entitlement to the carer element and that A shall not have an entitlement mentioned in paragraph (5)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc A and B jointly elect that B has the carer element and that A has no entitlement mentioned in paragraph (5)(a).
      `in default of election the Secretary of State is satisfied, following consultation with the Scottish Ministers, that the Scottish Ministers have decided or will decide that A shall not have an entitlement and that B shall have a carer element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In default of election, is the Secretary of State satisfied, following consultation with the Scottish Ministers, that they have decided or will decide that A has no such entitlement and that you have a carer element?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my award include the carer element when a Scottish entitlement is in question` IF
    `reg 29(6) — B's award may include the carer element` `the Scottish case`
    WHERE
        `the Scottish case` MEANS `Carer element where a Scottish entitlement is in question` WITH
            `person A has, or would have but for regulation 5(3) of the Carer's Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023, an entitlement to carer support payment` IS `person A has, or would have but for regulation 5(3) of the Carer's Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023, an entitlement to carer support payment`
            `person A has, or would have but for section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act, an entitlement to carer's allowance in respect of which the Scottish Ministers have the power to make decisions` IS `person A has, or would have but for section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act, an entitlement to carer's allowance in respect of which the Scottish Ministers have the power to make decisions`
            `person B has, or would have but for regulation 29, an entitlement to the carer element for the same day in respect of the same severely disabled person` IS `person B has, or would have but for regulation 29, an entitlement to the carer element for the same day in respect of the same severely disabled person`
            `section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act does not apply to the decision in respect of B's entitlement to universal credit` IS `section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act does not apply to the decision in respect of B's entitlement to universal credit`
            `A and B jointly elect that B shall have entitlement to the carer element and that A shall not have an entitlement mentioned in paragraph (5)(a)` IS `A and B jointly elect that B shall have entitlement to the carer element and that A shall not have an entitlement mentioned in paragraph (5)(a)`
            `in default of election the Secretary of State is satisfied, following consultation with the Scottish Ministers, that the Scottish Ministers have decided or will decide that A shall not have an entitlement and that B shall have a carer element` IS `in default of election the Secretary of State is satisfied, following consultation with the Scottish Ministers, that the Scottish Ministers have decided or will decide that A shall not have an entitlement and that B shall have a carer element`

-- reg 29. The three facts are the answers to the questions on regulation 29(1) to (3), (4) and (6).
@export How much carer element do I get, in pounds (reg 29)?
GIVEN `the carer element may be included for me by paragraphs (1) to (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 29(1) to (3) give the answer yes?
      `only the LCWRA element may be included for me under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 29(4) give the answer yes?
      `my award may include the carer element under paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 29(5), (6) give the answer yes?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much carer element do I get` IS
    `reg 29 — the amount of the carer element for a claimant` `the carer element may be included for me by paragraphs (1) to (3)` `only the LCWRA element may be included for me under paragraph (4)` `my award may include the carer element under paragraph (6)`

§§ `Childcare costs (regulations 31 to 35)`

-- reg 31. Yes where the work condition (regulation 32) and the childcare costs condition (regulation 33) are both met. The two facts are the answers to the questions on those regulations.
@export Does my award include the childcare costs element for an assessment period (reg 31)?
GIVEN `the work condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on the work condition (regulation 32(1)) give the answer yes?
      `the childcare costs condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on the childcare costs condition (regulation 33(1)) give the answer yes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my award include the childcare costs element for an assessment period` IF
    `reg 31 — the award includes the childcare costs element for the assessment period` `the work condition is met` `the childcare costs condition is met`

-- reg 32(2). Treated as in paid work if you ceased paid work in the assessment period in question, in the previous one, or (for the first or second assessment period of an award) in the month immediately before the award began; or if you are receiving statutory sick pay, statutory maternity pay, statutory paternity pay, statutory adoption pay, statutory shared parental pay, statutory parental bereavement pay, statutory neonatal care pay or a maternity allowance.
@export Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts (reg 32(2))?
GIVEN `my first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your first date of entitlement?
      `a day in the assessment period in question` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the assessment period you are asking about.
      `I have ceased paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased paid work?
      `the day I ceased paid work` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease paid work? (Any date if you have not.)
      `I am receiving a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving one of the payments mentioned in regulation 32(2)(b)?
      `the benefit I am receiving` IS A Benefit @desc Which payment are you receiving? (If more than one, choose any one.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` IF
    `reg 32(2) — the claimant is treated as being in paid work` (`reg 32(2)(a) — the claimant ceased paid work in time to be treated as in paid work` `my first date of entitlement` `a day in the assessment period in question` (IF `I have ceased paid work` THEN JUST `the day I ceased paid work` ELSE NOTHING)) (`reg 32(2)(b) — the claimant is receiving a payment that treats them as in paid work` (IF `I am receiving a benefit` THEN LIST `the benefit I am receiving` ELSE EMPTY))

-- reg 32(1). In paid work, or treated as in paid work, or with an offer of paid work starting before the end of the next assessment period; and, for a couple, the other member also in paid work or unable to provide childcare for one of the listed reasons.
@export Is the work condition for childcare costs met (reg 32(1))?
GIVEN `the claimant is in paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in paid work?
      `I am treated as being in paid work under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the previous question (regulation 32(2)) give the answer yes?
      `the claimant has an offer of paid work that is due to start before the end of the next assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an offer of paid work that is due to start before the end of the next assessment period?
      `the claimant is a member of a couple, whether claiming jointly or as a single person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple (whether claiming jointly or as a single person)?
      `the other member is in paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner in paid work?
      `the other member is unable to provide childcare because they have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner unable to provide childcare because they have limited capability for work?
      `the other member is unable to provide childcare because they have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner unable to provide childcare because they have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person?
      `the other member is unable to provide childcare because they are temporarily absent from the claimant's household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner unable to provide childcare because they are temporarily absent from your household?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the work condition for childcare costs met` IF
    `reg 32(1) — the work condition is met` `my work`
    WHERE
        `my work` MEANS `Facts for the work condition` WITH
            `the claimant is in paid work` IS `the claimant is in paid work`
            `the claimant is treated as being in paid work under paragraph (2)` IS `I am treated as being in paid work under paragraph (2)`
            `the claimant has an offer of paid work that is due to start before the end of the next assessment period` IS `the claimant has an offer of paid work that is due to start before the end of the next assessment period`
            `the claimant is a member of a couple, whether claiming jointly or as a single person` IS `the claimant is a member of a couple, whether claiming jointly or as a single person`
            `the other member is in paid work` IS `the other member is in paid work`
            `the other member is unable to provide childcare because they have limited capability for work` IS `the other member is unable to provide childcare because they have limited capability for work`
            `the other member is unable to provide childcare because they have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` IS `the other member is unable to provide childcare because they have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person`
            `the other member is unable to provide childcare because they are temporarily absent from the claimant's household` IS `the other member is unable to provide childcare because they are temporarily absent from the claimant's household`

-- reg 33(1)(za), (3). You must report the charges before the end of the assessment period after the one in which you paid them (the notification period), unless the Secretary of State accepts late reporting under regulation 36 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations 2013.
@export Have I paid my childcare charges and told the Secretary of State in time (reg 33(1)(za), (3))?
GIVEN `my first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your first date of entitlement?
      `I have paid charges for relevant childcare` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid charges for relevant childcare?
      `the day I paid the charges` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you pay the charges?
      `the day I reported the charges to the Secretary of State` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you report the charges to the Secretary of State?
      `late reporting is accepted under regulation 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State accepted late reporting under regulation 36 of the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Decisions and Appeals) Regulations 2013?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I paid my childcare charges and told the Secretary of State in time` IF
    `reg 33(1)(za) — the charges have been paid and reported in time` `my first date of entitlement` `I have paid charges for relevant childcare` `the day I paid the charges` `the day I reported the charges to the Secretary of State` `late reporting is accepted under regulation 36`

-- reg 33(3). The last day of the notification period: the last day of the assessment period after the one in which the charges were paid.
@export By what day must I tell the Secretary of State about my childcare charges (reg 33(3))?
GIVEN `my first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your first date of entitlement?
      `the day I paid the charges` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you pay (or will you pay) the charges?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I tell the Secretary of State about my childcare charges` IS
    `reg 33(3) — the last day of the relevant notification period` `my first date of entitlement` `the day I paid the charges`

@export Are my childcare charges for a child or young person I am responsible for (reg 33(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the person is a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person being cared for a child?
      `the person is a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person being cared for a qualifying young person?
      `date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the person's date of birth?
      `the claimant is responsible for the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you responsible for the person (see the question on regulation 4)?
      `first day of the assessment period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the assessment period you are asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my childcare charges for a child or young person I am responsible for` IF
    `reg 33(1)(a) — the charges are in respect of a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible` `the person cared for`
    WHERE
        `the person cared for` MEANS `Person for whom childcare charges are paid` WITH
            `the person is a child` IS `the person is a child`
            `the person is a qualifying young person` IS `the person is a qualifying young person`
            `date of birth` IS `date of birth`
            `the claimant is responsible for the person` IS `the claimant is responsible for the person`
            `first day of the assessment period` IS `first day of the assessment period`

@export Are my childcare charges for qualifying childcare arrangements (reg 33(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the arrangements enable me to take up paid work, or to remain in paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the arrangements enable you to take up paid work, or to remain in paid work?
      `I am treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated as being in paid work by regulation 32(2) (see the question on it)?
      `the arrangements enable me to maintain arrangements to take up or remain in paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the arrangements enable you to maintain arrangements for childcare so that you can take up or remain in paid work?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my childcare charges for qualifying childcare arrangements` IF
    `reg 33(1)(b) — the charges are for qualifying childcare arrangements` `the arrangements enable me to take up paid work, or to remain in paid work` `I am treated as being in paid work because I recently stopped or get a payment that counts` `the arrangements enable me to maintain arrangements to take up or remain in paid work`

-- reg 33(1). The three facts are the answers to the questions on regulation 33(1)(za), (a) and (b).
@export Is the childcare costs condition met (reg 33(1))?
GIVEN `the charges have been paid and reported in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 33(1)(za) give the answer yes?
      `the charges are for a child or young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 33(1)(a) give the answer yes?
      `the charges are for qualifying childcare arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 33(1)(b) give the answer yes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the childcare costs condition met` IF
    `reg 33(1) — the childcare costs condition is met` `the charges have been paid and reported in time` `the charges are for a child or young person I am responsible for` `the charges are for qualifying childcare arrangements`

-- reg 34A(1), (3). Charges are attributable to the assessment period in which they were paid if the care was provided in or before it, and to the period in which the care was provided if they were paid in either of the two periods before it. A month before the award began that starts on the same day as a period of the award counts as a period (paragraph (3)).
@export Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period (reg 34A(1))?
GIVEN `my first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your first date of entitlement?
      `the day I paid the charges` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you pay the charges?
      `a day in the period for which the childcare was provided` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the period for which the childcare was provided.
      `a day in the assessment period in question` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the assessment period you are asking about.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my childcare charges attributable to a given assessment period` IF
    `reg 34A(1) — the charges are attributable to the assessment period` `my first date of entitlement` `the day I paid the charges` `a day in the period for which the childcare was provided` `a day in the assessment period in question`

-- reg 34A(2). The source text shows the variables but not the formula (fork F-FORMULA), so the answer is always NOTHING.
@export How much of a childcare payment made in advance counts for an assessment period (reg 34A(2))?
GIVEN `the amount resulting from step 1, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount resulting from step 1, in pounds?
      `the total number of days covered by the payment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in total does the payment cover?
      `the number of days covered by the payment that also fall in the assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those days fall in the assessment period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of a childcare payment made in advance counts for an assessment period` IS
    `reg 34A(2) — the amount paid in advance in respect of an assessment period` `the amount resulting from step 1, in pounds` `the total number of days covered by the payment` `the number of days covered by the payment that also fall in the assessment period`

@export Is a payment I receive other relevant support, which is left out of account (reg 34(3))?
GIVEN `the payment is out of funds provided by the Secretary of State or by Scottish or Welsh Ministers in connection with the claimant's participation in work-related activity or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment out of funds provided by the Secretary of State or by Scottish or Welsh Ministers in connection with your taking part in work-related activity or training?
      `the payment is made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made by the Secretary of State?
      `the claimant has taken up, or is due to take up, paid work, or has increased, or is due to increase, their hours of paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken up, or are you due to take up, paid work, or increased (or are you due to increase) your hours of paid work?
      `the claimant is required to pay the charges for relevant childcare before they receive a payment of universal credit that reflects the increase in the claimant's earned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to pay the childcare charges before you get a payment of Universal Credit that reflects the increase in your earned income?
      `if the payment is not taken into account the claimant will be less likely to continue in paid work or maintain the increase in hours of paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the payment were not taken into account, would you be less likely to continue in paid work or to maintain the increase in your hours?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a payment I receive other relevant support, which is left out of account` IF
    `reg 34(3) — the payment is other relevant support` `my payment`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment that may be other relevant support` WITH
            `the payment is out of funds provided by the Secretary of State or by Scottish or Welsh Ministers in connection with the claimant's participation in work-related activity or training` IS `the payment is out of funds provided by the Secretary of State or by Scottish or Welsh Ministers in connection with the claimant's participation in work-related activity or training`
            `the payment is made by the Secretary of State` IS `the payment is made by the Secretary of State`
            `the claimant has taken up, or is due to take up, paid work, or has increased, or is due to increase, their hours of paid work` IS `the claimant has taken up, or is due to take up, paid work, or has increased, or is due to increase, their hours of paid work`
            `the claimant is required to pay the charges for relevant childcare before they receive a payment of universal credit that reflects the increase in the claimant's earned income` IS `the claimant is required to pay the charges for relevant childcare before they receive a payment of universal credit that reflects the increase in the claimant's earned income`
            `if the payment is not taken into account the claimant will be less likely to continue in paid work or maintain the increase in hours of paid work` IS `if the payment is not taken into account the claimant will be less likely to continue in paid work or maintain the increase in hours of paid work`

-- reg 34(2). The charges paid for relevant childcare attributable to the period, less any amount the Secretary of State considers excessive and any amount met or reimbursed by an employer or another person or covered by other relevant support.
@export How much of my childcare charges count after amounts are left out, in pounds (reg 34(2))?
GIVEN `the charges I paid for relevant childcare attributable to the assessment period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you pay in charges for relevant childcare attributable to the assessment period, in pounds?
      `the amount the Secretary of State considers excessive, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the charges, if any, does the Secretary of State consider excessive, in pounds?
      `the amount met or reimbursed by an employer or someone else, or covered by other relevant support, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the charges, if any, was met or reimbursed by an employer or another person, or is covered by other relevant support (see the question on regulation 34(3)), in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my childcare charges count after amounts are left out` IS
    `reg 34(2) — the charges paid after amounts are left out of account` `the charges I paid for relevant childcare attributable to the assessment period, in pounds` `the amount the Secretary of State considers excessive, in pounds` `the amount met or reimbursed by an employer or someone else, or covered by other relevant support, in pounds`

-- reg 34(1). 85% of the charges that count, but not more than the maximum for the number of children (regulation 36); NOTHING where the number of children is not 1 or more.
@export How much is my childcare costs element for an assessment period, in pounds (reg 34(1))?
GIVEN `the charges that count after amounts are left out, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your childcare charges count after amounts are left out, in pounds (see the previous question)?
      `the number of children for whom I pay childcare charges` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many children do you pay childcare charges?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my childcare costs element for an assessment period` IS
    `reg 34(1) — the amount of the childcare costs element for an assessment period` `the charges that count after amounts are left out, in pounds` `the number of children for whom I pay childcare charges`

-- reg 35(1), (2), (6), (7). Care in England counts if given by a person registered under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006, by a school or under its direction (in the cases the regulation lists), or by a domiciliary care provider registered with the Care Quality Commission; it does not count if given by a close relative wholly or mainly in the child's home or by the child's foster parent, or, under (2)(a), if given in breach of a requirement to register.
@export Is my childcare in England relevant childcare (reg 35(1), (2), (6), (7))?
GIVEN `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person cared for a child, or a qualifying young person within regulation 33(1)(a)(ii)?
      `the care is by a person registered under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a person registered under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006?
      `the care is provided in breach of a requirement to register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care provided in breach of a requirement to register under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006?
      `the care is provided as part of the school's activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care provided as part of a school's activities?
      `the school is one that the Chief Inspector must or may inspect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a school that the Chief Inspector of Education, Children's Services and Skills is, or may be, required to inspect?
      `the care is out of school hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care out of school hours?
      `the child has reached compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child reached compulsory school age?
      `the care is by a domiciliary care provider registered with the Care Quality Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a domiciliary care provider registered with the Care Quality Commission in accordance with the Health and Social Care Act 2008?
      `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home?
      `the care is provided by the child's foster parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a person who is a foster parent of the child?
      `the care is by or under the direction of the governing body of the school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by or under the direction of the governing body incorporated under section 19 of the Education Act 2002?
      `the school has no such governing body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the school have no such governing body?
      `the care is by or under the direction of the people responsible for managing the school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by or under the direction of the person or body of persons responsible for the management of the school?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my childcare in England relevant childcare` IF
    `reg 35(1) — the care is relevant childcare` `my care` (`reg 35(6)(a) — the care is by or under the direction of the proprietor of the school` `the care is by or under the direction of the governing body of the school` `the school has no such governing body` `the care is by or under the direction of the people responsible for managing the school`)
    WHERE
        `my care` MEANS `Care that may be relevant childcare` WITH
            `where the care is provided` IS `in England`
            `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person mentioned in regulation 33(1)(a)(ii)` IS `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person`
            `the care is by a person registered under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006` IS `the care is by a person registered under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006`
            `the care is provided in breach of a requirement to register under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006` IS `the care is provided in breach of a requirement to register`
            `the care is provided as part of the school's activities` IS `the care is provided as part of the school's activities`
            `the school is one that the Chief Inspector of Education, Children's Services and Skills is, or may be, required to inspect` IS `the school is one that the Chief Inspector must or may inspect`
            `the care is out of school hours` IS `the care is out of school hours`
            `the child has reached compulsory school age` IS `the child has reached compulsory school age`
            `the care is by a domiciliary care provider registered with the Care Quality Commission in accordance with the requirements of the Health and Social Care Act 2008` IS `the care is by a domiciliary care provider registered with the Care Quality Commission`
            `the care is by a person whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children within the meaning of schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010 and is registered under Part 5 of that Act` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a childcare agency whose care service consists of or includes supplying, or introducing to persons who use the service, childcarers within the meaning of paragraph 5 of schedule 12 to that Act` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a local authority whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children within the meaning of schedule 12 to that Act and is registered under Part 5 of that Act` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a person registered under Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `but for article 11, 12 or 14 of the Child Minding and Day Care Exceptions (Wales) Order 2010 the care would be day care for the purposes of Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a childcare provider approved in accordance with a scheme made under section 12(5) of the Tax Credits Act 2002 or under section 60 of the Government of Wales Act 2006` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a school on school premises, meaning premises that may be inspected as part of an inspection of the school` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a local authority` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a person employed, or engaged under a contract for services, to provide care and support by the provider of a domiciliary support service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a foster parent in relation to a child other than one whom the foster parent is fostering, and would be child minding or day care for the purposes of Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010 but for the fact that the child is over the age of the children to whom that Measure applies` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a childcare provider approved by an organisation accredited by the Secretary of State` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home` IS `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home`
            `the care is provided by a person who is a foster parent of the child` IS `the care is provided by the child's foster parent`

-- The module rule also reads a fact about a school proprietor, which only the rules for England use; FALSE is passed for it here.
-- reg 35(3). Care in Scotland counts if given by a registered childminder or day-care provider, a childcare agency, or a local authority service registered under Part 5 of the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010.
@export Is my childcare in Scotland relevant childcare (reg 35(1), (3), (7))?
GIVEN `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person cared for a child, or a qualifying young person within regulation 33(1)(a)(ii)?
      `the care is by a registered child minding or day care provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a person whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children (schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010) and is registered under Part 5 of that Act?
      `the care is by a registered childcare agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a childcare agency whose care service consists of or includes supplying, or introducing to people who use the service, childcarers?
      `the care is by a local authority service registered under Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a local authority whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children and is registered under Part 5 of that Act?
      `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home?
      `the care is provided by the child's foster parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a person who is a foster parent of the child?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my childcare in Scotland relevant childcare` IF
    `reg 35(1) — the care is relevant childcare` `my care` FALSE
    WHERE
        `my care` MEANS `Care that may be relevant childcare` WITH
            `where the care is provided` IS `in Scotland`
            `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person mentioned in regulation 33(1)(a)(ii)` IS `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person`
            `the care is by a person registered under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is provided in breach of a requirement to register under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is provided as part of the school's activities` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the school is one that the Chief Inspector of Education, Children's Services and Skills is, or may be, required to inspect` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is out of school hours` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the child has reached compulsory school age` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a domiciliary care provider registered with the Care Quality Commission in accordance with the requirements of the Health and Social Care Act 2008` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a person whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children within the meaning of schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010 and is registered under Part 5 of that Act` IS `the care is by a registered child minding or day care provider`
            `the care is by a childcare agency whose care service consists of or includes supplying, or introducing to persons who use the service, childcarers within the meaning of paragraph 5 of schedule 12 to that Act` IS `the care is by a registered childcare agency`
            `the care is by a local authority whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children within the meaning of schedule 12 to that Act and is registered under Part 5 of that Act` IS `the care is by a local authority service registered under Part 5`
            `the care is by a person registered under Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `but for article 11, 12 or 14 of the Child Minding and Day Care Exceptions (Wales) Order 2010 the care would be day care for the purposes of Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a childcare provider approved in accordance with a scheme made under section 12(5) of the Tax Credits Act 2002 or under section 60 of the Government of Wales Act 2006` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a school on school premises, meaning premises that may be inspected as part of an inspection of the school` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a local authority` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a person employed, or engaged under a contract for services, to provide care and support by the provider of a domiciliary support service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a foster parent in relation to a child other than one whom the foster parent is fostering, and would be child minding or day care for the purposes of Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010 but for the fact that the child is over the age of the children to whom that Measure applies` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a childcare provider approved by an organisation accredited by the Secretary of State` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home` IS `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home`
            `the care is provided by a person who is a foster parent of the child` IS `the care is provided by the child's foster parent`

-- The module rule also reads a fact about a school proprietor, which only the rules for England use; FALSE is passed for it here.
-- reg 35(4). Care in Wales counts if given by a person registered under Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010 or within the exceptions the regulation lists.
@export Is my childcare in Wales relevant childcare (reg 35(1), (4), (7))?
GIVEN `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person cared for a child, or a qualifying young person within regulation 33(1)(a)(ii)?
      `the care is out of school hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care out of school hours?
      `the care is by a person registered under Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a person registered under Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010?
      `it would be day care but for article 11, 12 or 14 of the Child Minding and Day Care Exceptions (Wales) Order 2010` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for article 11, 12 or 14 of the Child Minding and Day Care Exceptions (Wales) Order 2010, would the care be day care for the purposes of Part 2 of that Measure?
      `the care is by a childcare provider approved under a scheme under the Tax Credits Act 2002 or the Government of Wales Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a childcare provider approved in accordance with a scheme made under section 12(5) of the Tax Credits Act 2002 or under section 60 of the Government of Wales Act 2006?
      `the care is by a school on school premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a school on school premises (premises that may be inspected as part of an inspection of the school)?
      `the care is by a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a local authority?
      `the care is by a person engaged by a domiciliary support service in Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a person employed, or engaged under a contract for services, to provide care and support by the provider of a domiciliary support service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016?
      `the care is by a foster parent for a child other than one they are fostering` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a foster parent for a child other than one they are fostering, which would be child minding or day care under Part 2 of the Measure but for the child being over the age of the children to whom the Measure applies?
      `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home?
      `the care is provided by the child's foster parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a person who is a foster parent of the child?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my childcare in Wales relevant childcare` IF
    `reg 35(1) — the care is relevant childcare` `my care` FALSE
    WHERE
        `my care` MEANS `Care that may be relevant childcare` WITH
            `where the care is provided` IS `in Wales`
            `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person mentioned in regulation 33(1)(a)(ii)` IS `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person`
            `the care is by a person registered under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is provided in breach of a requirement to register under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is provided as part of the school's activities` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the school is one that the Chief Inspector of Education, Children's Services and Skills is, or may be, required to inspect` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is out of school hours` IS `the care is out of school hours`
            `the child has reached compulsory school age` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a domiciliary care provider registered with the Care Quality Commission in accordance with the requirements of the Health and Social Care Act 2008` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a person whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children within the meaning of schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010 and is registered under Part 5 of that Act` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a childcare agency whose care service consists of or includes supplying, or introducing to persons who use the service, childcarers within the meaning of paragraph 5 of schedule 12 to that Act` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a local authority whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children within the meaning of schedule 12 to that Act and is registered under Part 5 of that Act` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a person registered under Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010` IS `the care is by a person registered under Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010`
            `but for article 11, 12 or 14 of the Child Minding and Day Care Exceptions (Wales) Order 2010 the care would be day care for the purposes of Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010` IS `it would be day care but for article 11, 12 or 14 of the Child Minding and Day Care Exceptions (Wales) Order 2010`
            `the care is by a childcare provider approved in accordance with a scheme made under section 12(5) of the Tax Credits Act 2002 or under section 60 of the Government of Wales Act 2006` IS `the care is by a childcare provider approved under a scheme under the Tax Credits Act 2002 or the Government of Wales Act 2006`
            `the care is by a school on school premises, meaning premises that may be inspected as part of an inspection of the school` IS `the care is by a school on school premises`
            `the care is by a local authority` IS `the care is by a local authority`
            `the care is by a person employed, or engaged under a contract for services, to provide care and support by the provider of a domiciliary support service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016` IS `the care is by a person engaged by a domiciliary support service in Wales`
            `the care is by a foster parent in relation to a child other than one whom the foster parent is fostering, and would be child minding or day care for the purposes of Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010 but for the fact that the child is over the age of the children to whom that Measure applies` IS `the care is by a foster parent for a child other than one they are fostering`
            `the care is by a childcare provider approved by an organisation accredited by the Secretary of State` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home` IS `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home`
            `the care is provided by a person who is a foster parent of the child` IS `the care is provided by the child's foster parent`

-- The module rule also reads a fact about a school proprietor, which only the rules for England use; FALSE is passed for it here.
-- reg 35(5). Care outside Great Britain counts if given by a childcare provider approved by an organisation accredited by the Secretary of State.
@export Is my childcare outside Great Britain relevant childcare (reg 35(1), (5), (7))?
GIVEN `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person cared for a child, or a qualifying young person within regulation 33(1)(a)(ii)?
      `the care is by a childcare provider approved by an organisation accredited by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a childcare provider approved by an organisation accredited by the Secretary of State?
      `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home?
      `the care is provided by the child's foster parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care given by a person who is a foster parent of the child?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my childcare outside Great Britain relevant childcare` IF
    `reg 35(1) — the care is relevant childcare` `my care` FALSE
    WHERE
        `my care` MEANS `Care that may be relevant childcare` WITH
            `where the care is provided` IS `anywhere outside Great Britain`
            `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person mentioned in regulation 33(1)(a)(ii)` IS `the person cared for is a child, or a qualifying young person`
            `the care is by a person registered under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is provided in breach of a requirement to register under Part 3 of the Childcare Act 2006` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is provided as part of the school's activities` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the school is one that the Chief Inspector of Education, Children's Services and Skills is, or may be, required to inspect` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is out of school hours` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the child has reached compulsory school age` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a domiciliary care provider registered with the Care Quality Commission in accordance with the requirements of the Health and Social Care Act 2008` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a person whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children within the meaning of schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010 and is registered under Part 5 of that Act` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a childcare agency whose care service consists of or includes supplying, or introducing to persons who use the service, childcarers within the meaning of paragraph 5 of schedule 12 to that Act` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a local authority whose care service consists of child minding or of day care of children within the meaning of schedule 12 to that Act and is registered under Part 5 of that Act` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a person registered under Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `but for article 11, 12 or 14 of the Child Minding and Day Care Exceptions (Wales) Order 2010 the care would be day care for the purposes of Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a childcare provider approved in accordance with a scheme made under section 12(5) of the Tax Credits Act 2002 or under section 60 of the Government of Wales Act 2006` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a school on school premises, meaning premises that may be inspected as part of an inspection of the school` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a local authority` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a person employed, or engaged under a contract for services, to provide care and support by the provider of a domiciliary support service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a foster parent in relation to a child other than one whom the foster parent is fostering, and would be child minding or day care for the purposes of Part 2 of the Children and Families (Wales) Measure 2010 but for the fact that the child is over the age of the children to whom that Measure applies` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the rules called below do not read this field
            `the care is by a childcare provider approved by an organisation accredited by the Secretary of State` IS `the care is by a childcare provider approved by an organisation accredited by the Secretary of State`
            `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home` IS `the care is provided by a close relative of the child, wholly or mainly in the child's home`
            `the care is provided by a person who is a foster parent of the child` IS `the care is provided by the child's foster parent`

§§ `What the elements are worth, and a death in the household (regulations 36 and 37)`

-- reg 36(1), table. £338.58 or £424.90 for a single claimant, according to age; £528.34 or £666.97 for joint claimants, according to the ages of both.
@export What is my standard allowance for an assessment period, in pounds (reg 36(1))?
GIVEN `how I claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc How are you claiming (as a single claimant, as joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple)?
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years, on the first day of the assessment period?
      `my partner's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is your partner, in complete years, on the first day of the assessment period? (Any number if you are not joint claimants.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my standard allowance for an assessment period` IS
    `reg 36(1) — the standard allowance` `how I claim` `my age in years` `my partner's age in years`

@export What is the additional amount for a disabled child or young person, in pounds (reg 36(1))?
GIVEN `the rate that applies` IS A `Rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` @desc Which rate applies (the lower rate, the higher rate, or no additional amount; see the question on regulation 24(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the additional amount for a disabled child or young person` IS
    `reg 36(1) — the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `the rate that applies`

-- reg 36(1), table. £429.80 for a pre-2026 claimant, a severe conditions criteria claimant or a claimant who is terminally ill; otherwise £217.26.
@export What is my LCWRA element for an assessment period, in pounds (reg 36(1))?
GIVEN `I am a pre-2026 claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on regulation 27A(1) give the answer yes?
      `I am a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been determined that you are a severe conditions criteria claimant?
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `the months within which my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many months can your death in consequence of that disease reasonably be expected? (Any number if there is no progressive disease.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my LCWRA element for an assessment period` IS
    `reg 36(1) — the amount of the LCWRA element` `I am a pre-2026 claimant` `I am a severe conditions criteria claimant` `I am terminally ill`
    WHERE
        `my illness` MEANS Illness WITH
            `suffering from a progressive disease` IS `I suffer from a progressive disease`
            `months within which death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS `the months within which my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected`
        `I am terminally ill` MEANS
            `reg 2 — terminally ill` `my illness`

-- reg 36(1), table. £1,071.09 for one child, £1,836.16 for two or more; NOTHING for none.
@export What is the most my childcare costs element can be, in pounds (reg 36(1))?
GIVEN `the number of children for whom I pay childcare charges` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many children do you pay childcare charges?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my childcare costs element can be` IS
    `reg 36(1) — the maximum amount of the childcare costs element` `the number of children for whom I pay childcare charges`

-- reg 37. After the death of one member of a couple, a child or qualifying young person, a severely disabled person cared for, or a non-dependant, the maximum amount is worked out as if they had not died for the assessment period of the death and the next two.
@export Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died (reg 37)?
GIVEN `the person who has died` IS A `Person whose death does not at once change the maximum amount of an award` @desc Who has died?
      `my first date of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is your first date of entitlement?
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the death occur?
      `a day in the assessment period for which the maximum amount is calculated` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the assessment period you are asking about.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my award still worked out as if someone in the household had not died` IF
    `reg 37 — the maximum amount is calculated as if the person had not died` `the person who has died` `my first date of entitlement` `the day of the death` `a day in the assessment period for which the maximum amount is calculated`
